return {
  ["creature.dispater.coa2014"]={title="Dispater",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 412 (33d10 + 231)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 17 | CON 25 | INT 25 | WIS 22 | CHA 24\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Dispater's darkvision.\n\nFear Aura\n\nWhen a creature starts their turn within 120 feet of Dispater, they must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or have the frightened condition until they leave the aura. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to this effect for 1 hour.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nDispater regains 20 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Dispater dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Dispater fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nDispater has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRust Metal\n\nAny nonmagical weapon or ammunition made of metal that hits Dispater corrodes. After its hit, the weapon or ammunition is destroyed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDispater makes four attacks using his Wrought- Iron Tower, Iron Column, or a combination of the two. He can replace one of the attacks with Superheat Metal (if available).\n\nWrought-Iron Tower\n\nmw 20 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (2d8 + 12) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage. Dispater may replace the bludgeoning damage with damage of a type that the target is vulnerable to instead.\n\nIron Column\n\nrs 15 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h21 (2d8 + 12) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage. Dispater may replace the bludgeoning damage with damage of a type that the target is vulnerable to instead.\n\nSuperheat Metal {@recharge 4}\n\nDispater targets a metal object he can see within 90 feet of him. The metal glows white-hot, burning all that touches it. If the object was held by a creature, the creature must succeed on a 23 Dexterity saving throw to drop the object or take 45 (10d8) fire damage. If the object is attached to a creature, or they couldn't feasibly drop it, they automatically fail the save. The object returns to room temperature at the end of Dispater's turn.\n\nNail Spray (2/Day)\n\nDispater conjures a storm of iron nails and launches them forward in a 90-foot-long, 5-foot-wide line. All creatures within the line must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw, taking 40 (16d4) piercing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Nails launched from this ability stick into soft surfaces or fall to the ground after the attack finishes.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nStaff\n\nDispater makes a Wrought-Iron Tower attack.\n\nFlesh to Iron (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nms 15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h40 (6d10 + 7) force damage, and the target must make a 23 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target's flesh begins to harden, and the creature's movement speed is halved for 1 minute. If the creature is harmed by Flesh to Iron again, while still partly iron, the rest of the creature also turns to iron, killing them.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nDispater summons an allied erinyes in an unoccupied space that he can see."},
  ["spell.dispel-evil-and-good.phb2014"]={title="Dispel Evil and Good",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\nShimmering energy surrounds and protects you from fey, undead, and creatures originating from beyond the Material Plane. For the duration, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead have disadvantage on attack rolls against you.\n\nYou can end the spell early by using either of the following special functions.\n\nBreak Enchantment\n\nAs your action, you touch a creature you can reach that is charmed, frightened, or possessed by a celestial, an elemental, a fey, a fiend, or an undead. The creature you touch is no longer charmed, frightened, or possessed by such creatures.\n\nDismissal\n\nAs your action, make a melee spell attack against a celestial, an elemental, a fey, a fiend, or an undead you can reach. On a hit, you attempt to drive the creature back to its home plane. The creature must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be sent back to its home plane (if it isn't there already). If they aren't on their home plane, undead are sent to the Shadowfell, and fey are sent to the Feywild."},
  ["spell.dispel-evil-and-good.xphb2024"]={title="Dispel Evil and Good",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 263\n\nFor the duration, Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, and Undead have XPHB on attack rolls against you. You can end the spell early by using either of the following special functions.\n\nBreak Enchantment\n\nAs a XPHB action, you touch a creature that is possessed by or has the XPHB or XPHB condition from one or more creatures of the types above. The target is no longer possessed, XPHB, or XPHB by such creatures.\n\nDismissal\n\nAs a XPHB action, you target one creature you can see within 5 feet of you that has one of the creature types above. The target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be sent back to its home plane if it isn't there already. If they aren't on their home plane, Undead are sent to the Shadowfell, and Fey are sent to the Feywild."},
  ["spell.dispel-magic.phb2014"]={title="Dispel Magic",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nChoose one creature, object, or magical effect within range. Any spell of 3rd level or lower on the target ends. For each spell of 4th level or higher on the target, make an ability check using your spellcasting ability. The DC equals 10 + the spell's level. On a successful check, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.dispel-magic.xphb2024"]={title="Dispel Magic",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 264\n\nChoose one creature, object, or magical effect within range. Any ongoing spell of level 3 or lower on the target ends. For each ongoing spell of level 4 or higher on the target, make an ability check using your spellcasting ability (10 plus that spell's level). On a successful check, the spell ends."},
  ["feature.dispelling-recovery.au2014.cleric.arcana.6"]={title="Dispelling Recovery",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.dispelling-stone.egw2014"]={title="Dispelling Stone",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis smooth, rainbow-colored, egg-shaped stone can be thrown up to 30 feet and explodes in a 10-foot-radius sphere of magical energy on impact, destroying the stone. Any active spell of 5th level or lower in the sphere ends."},
  ["creature.displacer-beast.mm2014"]={title="Displacer Beast",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAvoidance\n\nIf the displacer beast is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a saving throw to take only half damage, it instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if it fails.\n\nDisplacement\n\nThe displacer beast projects a magical illusion that makes it appear to be standing near its actual location, causing attack rolls against it to have disadvantage. If it is hit by an attack, this trait is disrupted until the end of its next turn. This trait is also disrupted while the displacer beast is incapacitated or has a speed of 0.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe displacer beast makes two attacks with its tentacles.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.displacer-beast.xmm2024"]={title="Displacer Beast",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 76 (9d10 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Sylvan but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAvoidance\n\nIf the displacer beast is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a saving throw to take only half damage, it instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the save and half damage if it fails. It can't use this trait if it has the XPHB condition.\n\nDisplacement\n\nAttack rolls against the displacer beast have XPHB, since it projects an illusion that makes it appear to be near its actual location. This trait is suppressed while the displacer beast has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe displacer beast makes one Rend attack and one Tentacle attack.\n\nRend\n\nm 6, reach 5 feet. h9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage. If target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nTentacle\n\nm 6, reach 10 feet. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.displacer-beast-kitten.wbtw2014"]={title="Displacer Beast Kitten",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDisplacement\n\nThe displacer beast projects a magical illusion that makes it appear to be standing near its actual location, causing attack rolls against it to have disadvantage. If it is hit by an attack, this trait is disrupted until the end of its next turn. This trait is also disrupted while the displacer beast is incapacitated or has a speed of 0.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 bludgeoning damage plus 2 piercing damage."},
  ["creature.displacer-fiend.coa2014"]={title="Displacer Fiend",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 135 (18d10 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 19 | CON 14 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAvoidance\n\nIf the displacer fiend is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a saving throw to take only half damage, it instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if it fails.\n\nDisplacement\n\nThe displacer fiend projects a magical illusion that makes it appear to be standing near its actual location, causing attack rolls against it to have disadvantage. If it is hit by an attack, this trait is disrupted until the end of its next turn. This trait is also disrupted while the displacer fiend is incapacitated or has a speed of 0.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe displacer fiend makes three Tentacle attacks. It can replace one of the attacks with a Bite attack.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h23 (3d12 + 4) piercing damage, and the target's Dexterity score is reduced by 2 (1d4). The target is killed if this reduces its Dexterity to 0. The reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShadowhop\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the displacer fiend can teleport up to 60 feet, provided its destination is also in dim light or darkness."},
  ["spell.disruptive-tune.au2014"]={title="Disruptive Tune",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nA distracting melody momentarily fills a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point you choose within range. Each creature in the XPHB makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a target loses XPHB, and it has XPHB on Constitution saving throws to maintain XPHB for the spell's duration."},
  ["spell.dissonant-whispers.phb2014"]={title="Dissonant Whispers",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nYou whisper a discordant melody that only one creature of your choice within range can hear, wracking it with terrible pain. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 3d6 psychic damage and must immediately use its reaction, if available, to move as far as its speed allows away from you. The creature doesn't move into obviously dangerous ground, such as a fire or a pit. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage and doesn't have to move away. A deafened creature automatically succeeds on the save."},
  ["spell.dissonant-whispers.xphb2024"]={title="Dissonant Whispers",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 264\n\nOne creature of your choice that you can see within range hears a discordant melody in its mind. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 3d6 Psychic damage and must immediately use its XPHB, if available, to move as far away from you as it can, using the safest route. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["magicitem.dissuader.au2014"]={title="Dissuader",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis staff can be wielded as a magic XPHB that grants a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. It also has the following additional properties. Once one of these properties is used, that property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nCalm Emotions\n\nYou can cast the XPHB spell (save 15) from the staff.\n\nDissuading Aura\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding the staff, you can create a 30-foot XPHB of mental unrest originating from you that lasts for 1 minute. Whenever the XPHB enters the space of a creature you can see and whenever a creature you can see enters the XPHB or ends its turn there, you can force that creature to make a 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature has the XPHB condition until the start of its next turn.\n\nRepel\n\nWhen a creature enters a space within 5 feet of you, you can take a XPHB to create a shock wave of force. Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot XPHB originating from you must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 30 feet straight away from you."},
  ["optionalfeature.distant-spell.phb2014"]={title="Distant Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nWhen you cast a spell that has a range of 5 feet or greater, you can spend 1 sorcery point to double the range of the spell.\n\nWhen you cast a spell that has a range of touch, you can spend 1 sorcery point to make the range of the spell 30 feet."},
  ["optionalfeature.distant-spell.xphb2024"]={title="Distant Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 141\n\nWhen you cast a spell that has a range of at least 5 feet, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to double the spell's range. Or when you cast a spell that has a range of Touch, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to make the spell's range 30 feet."},
  ["feature.distant-strike.xge2024.ranger.horizon-walker.11"]={title="Distant Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 42\n\nAt 11th level, you gain the ability to pass between the planes in the blink of an eye. When you take the Attack action, you can teleport up to 10 feet before each attack to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\nIf you attack at least two different creatures with the action, you can make one additional attack with it against a third creature."},
  ["feature.distant-transposition.au2014.wizard.conjurer.6"]={title="Distant Transposition",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nThe range of your Benign Transposition feature increases to 60 feet. Additionally, you can restore one use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required)."},
  ["creature.distended-corpse.cos2014"]={title="Distended Corpse",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSnake-Swollen\n\nWhen a corpse is reduced to 0 hit points, it splits open, disgorging a swarm of poisonous snakes. The snakes are hungry and fight until slain."},
  ["spell.distort-value.ai2014"]={title="Distort Value",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 75\n\nDo you need to squeeze a few more gold pieces out of a merchant as you try to sell that weird octopus statue you liberated from the chaos temple? Do you need to downplay the worth of some magical assets when the tax collector stops by? Distort value has you covered.\n\nYou cast this spell on an object no more than 1 foot on a side, doubling the object's perceived value by adding illusory flourishes or polish to it, or reducing its perceived value by half with the help of illusory scratches, dents, and other unsightly features. Anyone examining the object can ascertain its true value with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC."},
  ["spell.distorted-distance.au2014"]={title="Distorted Distance",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nYou create an illusory spatial dilation that fills a 60-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within range. For each creature you can see in the XPHB, you can choose one of the following effects for it:\n\n• Dizzying Elongation The creature makes an Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 2d10 Psychic damage, and the XPHB is XPHB for it until the end of its turn.\n\n• Shortened Space The creature's XPHB increases by 20 feet until the end of its next turn. Until the spell ends, whenever a creature enters the XPHB or ends its turn there, you can choose for it to receive one of these effects. A creature can be affected by this spell only once per turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.distracting-strike.phb2014"]={title="Distracting Strike",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to distract the creature, giving your allies an opening. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll. The next attack roll against the target by an attacker other than you has advantage if the attack is made before the start of your next turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.distracting-strike.xphb2024"]={title="Distracting Strike",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 95\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can expend one Superiority Die to distract the target. Add the Superiority Die roll to the attack's damage roll. The next attack roll against the target by an attacker other than you has XPHB if the attack is made before the start of your next turn."},
  ["creature.diva.jttrc2014"]={title="Diva",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two melee attacks.\n\nBroken Bottle\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.diva-luma.jttrc2014"]={title="Diva Luma",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 71\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDiva Luma makes two high-heeled shoe attacks.\n\nHigh-Heeled Shoe\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.divination.phb2014"]={title="Divination",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nYour magic and an offering put you in contact with a god or a god's servants. You ask a single question concerning a specific goal, event, or activity to occur within 7 days. The DM offers a truthful reply. The reply might be a short phrase, a cryptic rhyme, or an omen.\n\nThe spell doesn't take into account any possible circumstances that might change the outcome, such as the casting of additional spells or the loss or gain of a companion.\n\nIf you cast the spell two or more times before finishing your next long rest, there is a cumulative 25 chance for each casting after the first that you get a random reading. The DM makes this roll in secret."},
  ["spell.divination.xphb2024"]={title="Divination",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 264\n\nThis spell puts you in contact with a god or a god's servants. You ask one question about a specific goal, event, or activity to occur within 7 days. The DM offers a truthful reply, which might be a short phrase or cryptic rhyme. The spell doesn't account for circumstances that might change the answer, such as the casting of other spells.\n\nIf you cast the spell more than once before finishing a XPHB, there is a cumulative 25 chance for each casting after the first that you get no answer."},
  ["feat.divination-adept.au2014"]={title="Divination Adept",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAdditional Spells\n\nYour prowess allows you to always have certain spells at the ready. When you have spell slots of a level specified in the Divination Adept Spells table, you thereafter always have the spells listed for that level and lower prepared.\n\nPrescient Intervention\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself makes a XPHB, you can take a XPHB to give that creature XPHB or XPHB (your choice) on that roll.\n\nOnce you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB. You can also regain use of this feature when you cast a spell from the Divination school using a spell slot.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Spell\n\n1 | XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feature.divination-savant.phb2014.wizard.divination.2"]={title="Divination Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a divination spell into your spellbook is halved."},
  ["feature.divination-savant.xphb2024.wizard.diviner.3"]={title="Divination Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 173\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots."},
  ["feature.divine-allegiance.scag2014.paladin.crown.7"]={title="Divine Allegiance",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nStarting at 7th level, when a creature within 5 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to magically substitute your own health for that of the target creature, causing that creature not to take the damage. Instead, you take the damage. This damage to you can't be reduced or prevented in any way."},
  ["feature.divine-domain.phb2014.cleric.base.1"]={title="Divine Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nChoose one domain related to your deity from the list of available domains. Each domain is detailed in their own feature, and each one provides examples of gods associated with it. Your choice grants you domain spells and other features when you choose it at 1st level. It also grants you additional ways to use Channel Divinity when you gain that feature at 2nd level, and additional benefits at 6th, 8th, and 17th levels.\n\nDomain Spells\n\nEach domain has a list of spells—its domain spells—that you gain at the cleric levels noted in the domain description. Once you gain a domain spell, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.\n\nIf you have a domain spell that doesn't appear on the cleric spell list, the spell is nonetheless a cleric spell for you."},
  ["feature.divine-domain-feature.phb2014.cleric.base.2"]={title="Divine Domain feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain a feature from your Divine Domain."},
  ["feature.divine-domain-feature.phb2014.cleric.base.6"]={title="Divine Domain feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature from your Divine Domain."},
  ["feature.divine-domain-feature.phb2014.cleric.base.8"]={title="Divine Domain feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 8th level, you gain a feature from your Divine Domain."},
  ["feature.divine-domain-feature.phb2014.cleric.base.17"]={title="Divine Domain feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 17th level, you gain a feature from your Divine Domain."},
  ["spell.divine-favor.phb2014"]={title="Divine Favor",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nYour prayer empowers you with divine radiance. Until the spell ends, your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 radiant damage on a hit."},
  ["spell.divine-favor.xphb2024"]={title="Divine Favor",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nUntil the spell ends, your attacks with weapons deal an extra 1d4 Radiant damage on a hit."},
  ["feature.divine-foreknowledge.frhof2014.cleric.knowledge.17"]={title="Divine Foreknowledge",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nAs a XPHB, you magically expand your mind to the future. For 1 hour, you have XPHB on XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB. You can also restore your use of this feature by expending a level 6+ spell slot (no action required)."},
  ["feature.divine-fury.xge2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Divine Fury",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-fury.xphb2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Divine Fury",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-health.phb2014.paladin.base.3"]={title="Divine Health",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-intervention.phb2014.cleric.base.10"]={title="Divine Intervention",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you can call on your deity to intervene on your behalf when your need is great.\n\nImploring your deity's aid requires you to use your action. Describe the assistance you seek, and roll percentile dice. If you roll a number equal to or lower than your cleric level, your deity intervenes. The DM chooses the nature of the intervention; the effect of any cleric spell or cleric domain spell would be appropriate. If your deity intervenes, you can't use this feature again for 7 days. Otherwise, you can use it again after you finish a long rest.\n\nAt 20th level, your call for intervention succeeds automatically, no roll required."},
  ["feature.divine-intervention.xphb2024.cleric.base.10"]={title="Divine Intervention",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-intervention-improvement.phb2014.cleric.base.20"]={title="Divine Intervention Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 20th level, your call for intervention succeeds automatically, no roll required."},
  ["feature.divine-magic.xge2024.sorcerer.divine-soul.1"]={title="Divine Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYour link to the divine allows you to learn spells from the cleric class. When your Spellcasting feature lets you learn or replace a sorcerer cantrip or a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose the new spell from the cleric spell list or the sorcerer spell list. You must otherwise obey all the restrictions for selecting the spell, and it becomes a sorcerer spell for you.\n\nIn addition, choose an affinity for the source of your divine power: good, evil, law, chaos, or neutrality. You learn an additional spell based on that affinity, as shown below. It is a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against your number of sorcerer spells known. If you later replace this spell, you must replace it with a spell from the cleric spell list.\n\nAffinity | Spell\n\nGood | cure wounds\n\nEvil | inflict wounds\n\nLaw | bless\n\nChaos | bane\n\nNeutrality | protection from evil and good"},
  ["feature.divine-order.xphb2024.cleric.base.1"]={title="Divine Order",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 70\n\nYou have dedicated yourself to one of the following sacred roles of your choice."},
  ["feature.divine-reaper.rhw2014.cleric.grave.17"]={title="Divine Reaper",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-sense.phb2014.paladin.base.1"]={title="Divine Sense",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nThe presence of strong evil registers on your senses like a noxious odor, and powerful good rings like heavenly music in your ears. As an action, you can open your awareness to detect such forces. Until the end of your next turn, you know the location of any celestial, fiend, or undead within 60 feet of you that is not behind Cover. You know the type (celestial, fiend, or undead) of any being whose presence you sense, but not its identity (the vampire Count Strahd von Zarovich, for instance). Within the same radius, you also detect the presence of any place or object that has been consecrated or desecrated, as with the hallow spell.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier. When you finish a long rest, you regain all expended uses."},
  ["feature.divine-sense.xphb2024.paladin.base.3"]={title="Divine Sense",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-smite.phb2014.paladin.base.2"]={title="Divine Smite",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nStarting at 2nd level, when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one spell slot to deal radiant damage to the target, in addition to the weapon's damage. The extra damage is 2d8 for a 1st-level spell slot, plus 1d8 for each spell level higher than 1st, to a maximum of 5d8. The damage increases by 1d8 if the target is an undead or a fiend, to a maximum of 6d8."},
  ["spell.divine-smite.xphb2024"]={title="Divine Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nThe target takes an extra 2d8 Radiant damage from the attack. The damage increases by 1d8 if the target is a Fiend or an Undead."},
  ["subclass.divine-soul.xge2024.sorcerer.divine-soul.0"]={title="Divine Soul",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Divine Magic\n\nPagina: 50\n\nYour link to the divine allows you to learn spells from the cleric class. When your Spellcasting feature lets you learn or replace a sorcerer cantrip or a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose the new spell from the cleric spell list or the sorcerer spell list. You must otherwise obey all the restrictions for selecting the spell, and it becomes a sorcerer spell for you.\n\nIn addition, choose an affinity for the source of your divine power: good, evil, law, chaos, or neutrality. You learn an additional spell based on that affinity, as shown below. It is a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against your number of sorcerer spells known. If you later replace this spell, you must replace it with a spell from the cleric spell list.\n\nAffinity | Spell\n\nGood | cure wounds\n\nEvil | inflict wounds\n\nLaw | bless\n\nChaos | bane\n\nNeutrality | protection from evil and good\n\nNivel 1 - Divine Soul\n\nPagina: 50\n\nSometimes the spark of magic that fuels a sorcerer comes from a divine source that glimmers within the soul. Having such a blessed soul is a sign that your innate magic might come from a distant but powerful familial connection to a divine being. Perhaps your ancestor was an angel, transformed into a mortal and sent to fight in a god's name.\n\nOr your birth might align with an ancient prophecy, marking you as a servant of the gods or a chosen vessel of divine magic.\n\nA Divine Soul, with a natural magnetism, is seen as a threat by some religious hierarchies. As an outsider who commands sacred power, a Divine Soul can undermine an existing order by claiming a direct tie to the divine.\n\nIn some cultures, only those who can claim the power of a Divine Soul may command religious power. In these lands, ecclesiastical positions are dominated by a few bloodlines and preserved over generations.\n\nNivel 1 - Favored by the Gods\n\nPagina: 50\n\nStarting at 1st level, divine power guards your destiny. If you fail a saving throw or miss with an attack roll, you can roll 2d4 and add it to the total, possibly changing the outcome. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Divine Soul\n\nNivel 6 - Empowered Healing\n\nPagina: 50\n\nStarting at 6th level, the divine energy coursing through you can empower healing spells. Whenever you or an ally within 5 feet of you rolls dice to determine the number of hit points a spell restores, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll any number of those dice once, provided you aren't incapacitated. You can use this feature only once per turn.\n\nNivel 14 - Otherworldly Wings\n\nPagina: 50\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can use a bonus action to manifest a pair of spectral wings from your back. While the wings are present, you have a flying speed of 30 feet. The wings last until you're incapacitated, you die, or you dismiss them as a bonus action.\n\nThe affinity you chose for your Divine Magic feature determines the appearance of the spectral wings: eagle wings for good or law, bat wings for evil or chaos, and dragonfly wings for neutrality.\n\nNivel 18 - Unearthly Recovery\n\nPagina: 50\n\nAt 18th level, you gain the ability to overcome grievous injuries. As a bonus action when you have fewer than half of your hit points remaining, you can regain a number of hit points equal to half your hit point maximum.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.divine-soul.xge2024.sorcerer.divine-soul.1"]={title="Divine Soul",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 50\n\nSometimes the spark of magic that fuels a sorcerer comes from a divine source that glimmers within the soul. Having such a blessed soul is a sign that your innate magic might come from a distant but powerful familial connection to a divine being. Perhaps your ancestor was an angel, transformed into a mortal and sent to fight in a god's name.\n\nOr your birth might align with an ancient prophecy, marking you as a servant of the gods or a chosen vessel of divine magic.\n\nA Divine Soul, with a natural magnetism, is seen as a threat by some religious hierarchies. As an outsider who commands sacred power, a Divine Soul can undermine an existing order by claiming a direct tie to the divine.\n\nIn some cultures, only those who can claim the power of a Divine Soul may command religious power. In these lands, ecclesiastical positions are dominated by a few bloodlines and preserved over generations."},
  ["feature.divine-soul.xge2024.sorcerer.divine-soul.3"]={title="Divine Soul",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-spark.xphb2024.cleric.base.2"]={title="Divine Spark",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.dmg2014.cleric.death.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.phb2014.cleric.life.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.phb2014.cleric.nature.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.phb2014.cleric.tempest.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 thunder damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.phb2014.cleric.trickery.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.phb2014.cleric.war.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.psa2014.cleric.strength-psa.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.psa2014.cleric.zeal-psa.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.tce2014.cleric.order.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.tce2014.cleric.twilight.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n8th-level Twilight Domain feature\n\nYou gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."},
  ["feature.divine-strike.xge2024.cleric.forge.8"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.divine-strike.xphb2024.cleric.base.7"]={title="Divine Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.divine-word.phb2014"]={title="Divine Word",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 7 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nYou utter a divine word, imbued with the power that shaped the world at the dawn of creation. Choose any number of creatures you can see within range. Each creature that can hear you must make a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, a creature suffers an effect based on its current hit points:\n\n• 50 hit points or fewer: deafened for 1 minute\n\n• 40 hit points or fewer: deafened and blinded for 10 minutes\n\n• 30 hit points or fewer: blinded, deafened, and stunned for 1 hour\n\n• 20 hit points or fewer: killed instantly\n\nRegardless of its current hit points, a celestial, an elemental, a fey, or a fiend that fails its save is forced back to its plane of origin (if it isn't there already) and can't return to your current plane for 24 hours by any means short of a wish spell."},
  ["spell.divine-word.xphb2024"]={title="Divine Word",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 7 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nYou utter a word imbued with power from the Upper Planes. Each creature of your choice in range makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, a target that has 50 XPHB or fewer suffers an effect based on its current XPHB, as shown in the Divine Word Effects table. Regardless of its XPHB, a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend target that fails its save is forced back to its plane of origin (if it isn't there already) and can't return to the current plane for 24 hours by any means short of a XPHB spell.\n\nHit Points | Effect\n\n0-20 | The target dies.\n\n21-30 | The target has the XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB conditions for 1 hour.\n\n31-40 | The target has the XPHB and XPHB conditions for 10 minutes.\n\n41-50 | The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute."},
  ["feat.divinely-favored.dsotdq2014"]={title="Divinely Favored",subtitle="Feat - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nA god chose you to carry a spark of their power.\n\nYou learn one cantrip of your choice from the spells and one 1st-level spell based on the alignment of your character, as specified in the Alignment Spells table below. You also learn the augury spell.\n\nAlignment | 1st-Level Spell\n\nEvil | Choose one spells\n\nGood | Choose one spells\n\nNeutral | Choose one spells\n\nYou can cast the chosen 1st-level spell and the augury spell without a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast either of these spells in this way again. You can also cast these spells using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nYour spellcasting ability for this feat's spells is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).\n\nIn addition, you can use a holy symbol as a spellcasting focus for any spell you cast that uses the spellcasting ability you choose when you select this feat."},
  ["creature.diviner.vgm2014"]={title="Diviner",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 67 (15d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 18 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPortent (Recharges after the Diviner Casts a Divination Spell of 1st Level or Higher)\n\nWhen the diviner or a creature it can see makes an attack roll, a saving throw, or an ability check, the diviner can roll a d20 and choose to use this roll in place of the attack roll, saving throw, or ability check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands."},
  ["subclass.diviner.xphb2024.wizard.diviner.0"]={title="Diviner",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Divination Savant\n\nPagina: 173\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nNivel 3 - Diviner\n\nPagina: 173\n\nLearn the Secrets of the Multiverse\n\nThe counsel of a Diviner is sought by those who want a clearer understanding of the past, present, and future. As a Diviner, you strive to part the veils of space, time, and consciousness. You work to master spells of discernment, remote viewing, supernatural knowledge, and foresight.\n\nNivel 3 - Portent\n\nPagina: 173\n\nGlimpses of the future begin to press on your awareness. Whenever you finish a XPHB, roll two d20s and record the numbers rolled. You can replace any XPHB made by you or a creature that you can see with one of these foretelling rolls. You must choose to do so before the roll, and you can replace a roll in this way only once per turn.\n\nEach foretelling roll can be used only once. When you finish a XPHB, you lose any unused foretelling rolls.\n\nNivel 6 - Expert Divination\n\nPagina: 173\n\nCasting Divination spells comes so easily to you that it expends only a fraction of your spellcasting efforts. When you cast a Divination spell using a level 2+ spell slot, you regain one expended spell slot. The slot you regain must be of a level lower than the slot you expended and can't be higher than level 5.\n\nNivel 6 - Expert Divination\n\nNivel 10 - The Third Eye\n\nPagina: 173\n\nYou can increase your powers of perception. As a XPHB, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you start a XPHB or XPHB. You can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou gain XPHB with a range of 120 feet.\n\nGreater Comprehension\n\nYou can read any language.\n\nSee Invisibility\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot.\n\nNivel 10 - The Third Eye\n\nNivel 14 - Greater Portent\n\nPagina: 173\n\nThe visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. Roll three d20s for your Portent feature rather than two."},
  ["feature.diviner.xphb2024.wizard.diviner.3"]={title="Diviner",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 173\n\nLearn the Secrets of the Multiverse\n\nThe counsel of a Diviner is sought by those who want a clearer understanding of the past, present, and future. As a Diviner, you strive to part the veils of space, time, and consciousness. You work to master spells of discernment, remote viewing, supernatural knowledge, and foresight."},
  ["creature.diviner-archmage.au2014"]={title="Diviner Archmage",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 176 (32d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: all\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archmage has XPHB on saving throws against spells and similar effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archmage makes four Arcane Burst attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version).\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 10, reach 5 ft. or range 150 ft. h24 (3d12 + 5) Force damage."},
  ["creature.diviner-wizard.mpmm2014"]={title="Diviner Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 90 (20d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 18 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe diviner makes three Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) radiant damage.\n\nOverwhelming Revelation {@recharge 5}\n\nThe diviner magically creates a burst of illumination in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within 120 feet of it. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 45 (10d8) psychic damage and is stunned until the end of the diviner's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't stunned.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nPortent (3/Day)\n\nWhen the diviner or a creature it can see makes an attack roll, a saving throw, or an ability check, the diviner rolls a d20 and chooses whether to use that roll in place of the d20 rolled for the attack roll, saving throw, or ability check."},
  ["creature.djeneba.jttrc2014"]={title="Djeneba",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.djinni.mm2014"]={title="Djinni",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 161 (14d10 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 15 | CON 22 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran\n\nImunidades: lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nElemental Demise\n\nIf the djinni dies, its body disintegrates into a warm breeze, leaving behind only equipment the djinni was wearing or carrying.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe djinni makes three scimitar attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) lightning or thunder damage (djinni's choice).\n\nCreate Whirlwind\n\nA 5-foot-radius, 30-foot-tall cylinder of swirling air magically forms on a point the djinni can see within 120 feet of it. The whirlwind lasts as long as the djinni maintains concentration (as if concentration on a spell). Any creature but the djinni that enters the whirlwind must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be restrained by it. The djinni can move the whirlwind up to 60 feet as an action, and creatures restrained by the whirlwind move with it. The whirlwind ends if the djinni loses sight of it.\n\nA creature can use its action to free a creature restrained by the whirlwind, including itself, by succeeding on a 18 Strength check. If the check succeeds, the creature is no longer restrained and moves to the nearest space outside the whirlwind."},
  ["creature.djinni.xmm2024"]={title="Djinni",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 218 (19d10 + 114)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 15 | CON 22 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Auran)\n\nImunidades: lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nElemental Restoration\n\nIf the djinni dies outside the Elemental Plane of Air, its body dissolves into mist, and it gains a new body in 1d4 days, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere on the Plane of Air.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe djinni has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nWishes\n\nThe djinni has a 30 percent chance of knowing the XPHB spell. If the djinni knows it, the djinni can cast it only on behalf of a non-genie creature who communicates a wish in a way the djinni can understand. If the djinni casts the spell for the creature, the djinni suffers none of the spell's stress. Once the djinni has cast it three times, the djinni can't do so again for 365 days.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe djinni makes three attacks, using Storm Blade or Storm Bolt in any combination.\n\nStorm Blade\n\nm 9, reach 5 feet. h12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Lightning damage.\n\nStorm Bolt\n\nr 9, range 120 feet. h13 (3d8) Thunder damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nCreate Whirlwind\n\nThe djinni conjures a whirlwind at a point it can see within 120 feet. The whirlwind fills a 20-foot-radius, 60-foot-high XPHB centered on that point. The whirlwind lasts until the djinni's XPHB on it ends. The djinni can move the whirlwind up to 20 feet at the start of each of its turns.\n\nWhenever the whirlwind enters a creature's space or a creature enters the whirlwind, that creature is subjected to the following effect. str 17 (a creature makes this save only once per turn, and the djinni is unaffected). actSaveFail While in the whirlwind, the target has the XPHB condition and moves with the whirlwind. At the start of each of its turns, the XPHB target takes 21 (6d6) Thunder damage. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["feature.djinni-s-escape.frhof2014.paladin.noble-genies.3"]={title="Djinni's Escape",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nYou XPHB to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself and take on a semi-incorporeal form, which lasts until the end of your next turn. While in this form, you have XPHB to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage, and you have XPHB to the XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB conditions."},
  ["magicitem.docent.erlw2014"]={title="Docent",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA docent is a small metal sphere, about 2 inches across, studded with dragonshards. To attune to a docent, you must embed the item somewhere on your body, such as your chest or your eye socket.\n\nSentience\n\nA docent is a sentient item of any alignment with an Intelligence of 16, a Wisdom of 14, and a Charisma of 14. It perceives the world through your senses. It communicates telepathically with you and can speak, read, and understand any language it knows (see \"Random Properties\" below).\n\nLife Support\n\nWhenever you end your turn with 0 hit points, the docent can make a Wisdom (Medicine) check with a +6 bonus. If this check succeeds, the docent stabilizes you.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nA docent has the following properties:\n\nLanguages. The docent knows Common, Giant, and 1d4 additional languages chosen by the DM. If a docent knows fewer than six languages, it can learn a new language after it hears or reads the language through your senses.\n\nSkills. The docent has a +7 bonus to one of the following skills (roll a d4): (1) Arcana, (2) History, (3) Investigation, or (4) Nature.\n\nSpells. The docent knows one of the following spells and can cast it at will, requiring no components (roll a d6): (1–2) detect evil and good or (3–6) detect magic. The docent decides when to cast the spell.\n\nPersonality\n\nA docent is designed to advise and assist the warforged it's attached to. One of the simple functions of a docent is to serve as a translator. The docent's properties are under its control, and if you have a bad relationship with your docent, it might refuse to assist you."},
  ["magicitem.documancy-satchel.ai2014"]={title="Documancy Satchel",subtitle="Item Magico - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: varies\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nAt rank 2, your documancy satchel becomes a common magic item, allowing you to magically send and receive documents to and from Head Office through a special pouch. Your documancy satchel magically produces prewritten and signature-ready contracts at your request, covering most common contractual needs. It also occasionally produces sticky notes printed with useful information and inspirational quotes from Head Office.\n\nSatchel of Holding\n\nAt rank 3, your documancy satchel gains additional features and becomes an uncommon magic item. One of the satchel's pouches now functions as a bag of holding.\n\nAdditionally, you can use an action to draw forth from the documancy satchel a spell scroll of comprehend languages. The scroll vanishes when used, or ten minutes after it appears. This property of the bag can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nScroll Humidor\n\nAt rank 4, your documancy satchel gains additional power and becomes a rare magic item. Within the satchel, a dedicated extradimensional space can hold up to thirty documents or spell scroll. Placing a single document into the scroll humidor is an action. Drawing forth a desired scroll is a bonus action."},
  ["magicitem.dodecahedron-of-doom.wdmm2014"]={title="Dodecahedron of Doom",subtitle="Item Magico - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis twelve-sided metal die is 12 inches across and bears the numbers 1 through 12 engraved on its pentagonal sides. The dodecahedron contains arcane clockwork mechanisms that whir and click whenever the die is cast.\n\nThe dodecahedron can be hurled up to 60 feet as an action. A random magical effect occurs when the die comes to rest after rolling across the ground for at least 10 feet. If an effect requires a target and no eligible target is within range, nothing happens. Spells cast by the dodecahedron require no components. Roll a d12 and consult the following table to determine the effect:\n\nd12 | effect\n\n1–2 | The dodecahedron explodes and is destroyed. Each creature within 20 feet of the exploding die must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 40 (9d8) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n3–4 | The dodecahedron casts light on itself. The effect lasts until a creature touches the die.\n\n5–6 | The dodecahedron casts ray of frost (5 to hit), targeting a random creature within 60 feet of it that doesn't have Cover against the attack.\n\n7–8 | The dodecahedron casts shocking grasp (5 to hit) on the next creature that touches it.\n\n9–10 | The dodecahedron casts darkness on itself. The effect has a duration of 10 minutes.\n\n11–12 | The next creature to touch the dodecahedron gains 1d10 temporary hit points that last for 1 hour."},
  ["actionref.dodge.phb2014"]={title="Dodge",subtitle="Acao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nWhen you take the Dodge action, you focus entirely on avoiding attacks. Until the start of your next turn, any attack roll made against you has disadvantage if you can see the attacker, and you make Dexterity saving throws with advantage. You lose this benefit if you are incapacitated (as explained in the appendix) or if your speed drops to 0."},
  ["actionref.dodge.xphb2024"]={title="Dodge",subtitle="Acao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 366\n\nIf you take the Dodge action, you gain the following benefits: until the start of your next turn, any attack roll made against you has XPHB if you can see the attacker, and you make Dexterity XPHB with XPHB.\n\nYou lose these benefits if you have the XPHB condition or if your XPHB is 0."},
  ["item.dogsled.idrotf2014"]={title="Dogsled",subtitle="Item - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn empty sled costs 20 gp, weighs 300 pounds, and has room at the back for one driver."},
  ["creature.dohwar.bam2014"]={title="Dohwar",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 20\n\nSTR 5 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dohwar, telepathy 30 ft. (see also Merging below)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMerging\n\nTwo dohwars can have a telepathic conversation with each other and a third willing creature of their choice, provided all three are within 30 feet of one another.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["deity.dol-arrah.erlw2014"]={title="Dol Arrah",subtitle="Divindade - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nDol Arrah is the sun that drives away the darkness. She stands for wisdom in war and for those who fight with honor, pursue justice, and make sacrifices for the greater good."},
  ["deity.dol-arrah.phb2014"]={title="Dol Arrah",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["deity.dol-dorn.erlw2014"]={title="Dol Dorn",subtitle="Divindade - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nDol Dorn is the Sovereign of Strength and Steel. He is the patron of the common soldier, and he guides the hands of anyone who holds a weapon. He embodies courage, strength, and martial skill."},
  ["deity.dol-dorn.phb2014"]={title="Dol Dorn",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.dolgaunt.erlw2014"]={title="Dolgaunt",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 290\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Goblin\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf the dolgaunt is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, the dolgaunt instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if it fails. It can't use this trait if it's incapacitated.\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the dolgaunt is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dolgaunt makes two tentacle attacks and two unarmed strikes. Up to two tentacle attacks can be replaced by Vitality Drain.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. The target is grappled (escape 12) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until this grapple ends, the dolgaunt can't use the same tentacle on another target. The dolgaunt has two tentacles.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nVitality Drain\n\nOne creature grappled by a tentacle of the dolgaunt must make a 11 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 9 (2d8) necrotic damage, and the dolgaunt regains a number of hit points equal to half the necrotic damage taken."},
  ["creature.dolgrim.erlw2014"]={title="Dolgrim",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 291\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDual Consciousness\n\nThe dolgrim has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, and knocked unconscious.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dolgrim makes three attacks.\n\nMorningstar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.dolphin.mpmm2014"]={title="Dolphin",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 60\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe dolphin can hold its breath for 20 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage. If the dolphin moved at least 30 feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.dolphin.vgm2014"]={title="Dolphin",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 60\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the dolphin moves at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a slam attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe dolphin can hold its breath for 20 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.dolphin-delighter.mpmm2014"]={title="Dolphin Delighter",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 60\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, telepathy 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe dolphin can hold its breath for 20 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dolphin makes two Dazzling Slam attacks.\n\nDazzling Slam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage, and the target is blinded until the start of the dolphin's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDelightful Light {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dolphin magically emanates light in a 10-foot radius for a moment. The dolphin and each creature of its choice in that light gain 11 (2d10) temporary hit points.\n\nFey Leap\n\nThe dolphin teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. Immediately before teleporting, the dolphin can choose one creature within 5 feet of it. That creature can teleport with the dolphin, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the dolphin's destination space."},
  ["creature.domestic-wonder.fraif2014"]={title="Domestic Wonder",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 5 (1d8 + 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 8 | CON 13 | INT 3 | WIS 8 | CHA 1\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMechanical Determination\n\nIf damage reduces the wonder to 0 XPHB, it makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 plus the damage taken unless the damage is Lightning or from a XPHB. On a successful save, the wonder drops to 1 XPHB instead.\n\nWind-Up Operation\n\nThe wonder has the XPHB condition until another creature winds it with the wonder's unique key for 1 minute. Once wound, the wonder operates for 10 days or until a creature touches the wonder with its key as a XPHB action to deactivate it, after which the wonder has the XPHB condition until it is wound again."},
  ["spell.dominate-beast.phb2014"]={title="Dominate Beast",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\nYou attempt to beguile a beast that you can see within range. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by you for the duration. If you or creatures that are friendly to you are fighting it, it has advantage on the saving throw.\n\nWhile the beast is charmed, you have a telepathic link with it as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence. You can use this telepathic link to issue commands to the creature while you are conscious (no action required), which it does its best to obey. You can specify a simple and general course of action, such as \"Attack that creature,\" \"Run over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" If the creature completes the order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it defends and preserves itself to the best of its ability.\n\nYou can use your action to take total and precise control of the target. Until the end of your next turn, the creature takes only the actions you choose, and doesn't do anything that you don't allow it to do. During this time, you can also cause the creature to use a reaction, but this requires you to use your own reaction as well.\n\nEach time the target takes damage, it makes a new Wisdom saving throw against the spell. If the saving throw succeeds, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.dominate-beast.xphb2024"]={title="Dominate Beast",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nOne Beast you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration. The target has XPHB on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success.\n\nYou have a telepathic link with the XPHB target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as \"XPHB that creature,\" \"Move over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself.\n\nYou can command the target to take a XPHB but must take your own XPHB to do so."},
  ["spell.dominate-monster.phb2014"]={title="Dominate Monster",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\nYou attempt to beguile a creature that you can see within range. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by you for the duration. If you or creatures that are friendly to you are fighting it, it has advantage on the saving throw.\n\nWhile the creature is charmed, you have a telepathic link with it as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence. You can use this telepathic link to issue commands to the creature while you are conscious (no action required), which it does its best to obey. You can specify a simple and general course of action, such as \"Attack that creature,\" \"Run over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" If the creature completes the order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it defends and preserves itself to the best of its ability.\n\nYou can use your action to take total and precise control of the target. Until the end of your next turn, the creature takes only the actions you choose, and doesn't do anything that you don't allow it to do. During this time, you can also cause the creature to use a reaction, but this requires you to use your own reaction as well.\n\nEach time the target takes damage, it makes a new Wisdom saving throw against the spell. If the saving throw succeeds, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.dominate-monster.xphb2024"]={title="Dominate Monster",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nOne creature you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration. The target has XPHB on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success.\n\nYou have a telepathic link with the XPHB target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as \"XPHB that creature,\" \"Move over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself.\n\nYou can command the target to take a XPHB but must take your own XPHB to do so."},
  ["spell.dominate-person.phb2014"]={title="Dominate Person",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\nYou attempt to beguile a humanoid that you can see within range. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by you for the duration. If you or creatures that are friendly to you are fighting it, it has advantage on the saving throw.\n\nWhile the target is charmed, you have a telepathic link with it as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence. You can use this telepathic link to issue commands to the creature while you are conscious (no action required), which it does its best to obey. You can specify a simple and general course of action, such as \"Attack that creature,\" \"Run over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" If the creature completes the order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it defends and preserves itself to the best of its ability.\n\nYou can use your action to take total and precise control of the target. Until the end of your next turn, the creature takes only the actions you choose, and doesn't do anything that you don't allow it to do. During this time you can also cause the creature to use a reaction, but this requires you to use your own reaction as well.\n\nEach time the target takes damage, it makes a new Wisdom saving throw against the spell. If the saving throw succeeds, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.dominate-person.xphb2024"]={title="Dominate Person",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 266\n\nOne Humanoid you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration. The target has XPHB on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success.\n\nYou have a telepathic link with the XPHB target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as \"XPHB that creature,\" \"Move over there,\" or \"Fetch that object.\" The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn't receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself.\n\nYou can command the target to take a XPHB but must take your own XPHB to do so."},
  ["actionref.don-or-doff-a-shield.phb2014"]={title="Don or Doff a Shield",subtitle="Acao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\nThe time it takes to don or doff armor phb. A phb can be donned or doffed as an action."},
  ["actionref.don-or-doff-a-shield.xphb2024"]={title="Don or Doff a Shield",subtitle="Acao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nA XPHB can be donned or doffed as an action."},
  ["creature.don-jon-raskin.dip2014"]={title="Don-Jon Raskin",subtitle="Criatura - DIP - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 10 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nDon-Jon has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nNot Dead Yet (Recharges after a Long Rest)\n\nIf damage reduces Don-Jon to 0 hit points, he drops to 1 hit point instead and gains advantage on attack rolls until the end of his next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDon-Jon makes three melee attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.donaar-blit-zen.ai2014"]={title="Donaar Blit'zen",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Orc\n\nResistencias: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChampion Challenge (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, Donaar causes each creature of his choice that he can see within 30 feet of him to make a 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, a creature can't willingly move more than 30 feet away from Donaar. This effect ends on the creature if Donaar is incapacitated or dies, or if the creature is moved more than 30 feet away from him.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDonaar makes two attacks with his greatsword or his whip.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage. Whenever Donaar rolls a 1 or 2 on a damage die, he can reroll the die and must use the new roll.\n\nWhip\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nAcid Vomit\n\nDonaar regurgitates acid in a 30-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.donavich.cos2014"]={title="Donavich",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["magicitem.donjon-card.bmt2014"]={title="Donjon Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can brandish this card at one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a 17 Charisma saving throw, or it vanishes, transported to a prison on another plane of existence. After 1 minute, the target reappears in the space it left or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.donjon-s-sundering-sphere.bmt2014"]={title="Donjon's Sundering Sphere",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis marble-size crystal sphere glows with extraplanar energy.\n\nAs part of attuning to this item, you press the crystal sphere to the hilt of a nonmagical melee weapon of your choice, magically attaching the sphere to the weapon. The weapon becomes a magic weapon with a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. While wielding this weapon, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Dimensional Anchor You have advantage on saving throws against spells or effects that would send you to an extradimensional space, a demiplane, or another plane of existence against your will.\n\n• Isolating Smite When you hit a creature with this weapon, you can force the creature to make a 16 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is banished to a harmless demiplane until the end of its next turn. When the banished creature returns, it reappears in the space it left or the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nWhen you end your attunement to the sphere, the sphere harmlessly detaches from the weapon, and the weapon reverts to a nonmagical piece of equipment."},
  ["item.donkey.phb2014"]={title="Donkey",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.doomguard-doom-lord.mpp2014"]={title="Doomguard Doom Lord",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 15 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus three more languages\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Doom\n\nAny creature that starts its turn within 10 feet of the doom lord must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the doom lord doesn't have the incapacitated condition, it can suppress or resume this aura at the start of its turn (no action required).\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe doom lord deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe doom lord makes two Entropic Greatsword or Entropic Javelin attacks.\n\nEntropic Greatsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage. A creature killed by this attack has its body and everything it is wearing or carrying, except for magic items, reduced to ash.\n\nEntropic Javelin\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage. A creature killed by this attack has its body and everything it is wearing or carrying, except for magic items, reduced to ash."},
  ["creature.doomguard-rot-blade.mpp2014"]={title="Doomguard Rot Blade",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 97 (13d8 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two more languages\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe rot blade makes two Entropic Blade or Entropic Javelin attacks.\n\nEntropic Blade\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage. A creature killed by this attack has its body and everything it is wearing or carrying, except for magic items, reduced to ash. homThe rot blade can cause the blade to emit a burst of entropic magic in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on the weapon. Each creature in that area other than the rot blade must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 6 (1d12) necrotic damage. The blade can emit entropic magic in this way only once per turn.\n\nEntropic Javelin\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) necrotic damage. A creature killed by this attack has its body and everything it is wearing or carrying, except for magic items, reduced to ash."},
  ["spell.doomtide.frhof2014"]={title="Doomtide",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nYou create a 20-foot-radius XPHB of inky fog within range. The fog is magical XPHB and lasts for the duration or until a strong wind (such as the one created by the XPHB spell) disperses it, ending the spell.\n\nEach creature in the XPHB when it appears makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 5d6 Psychic damage and subtracts 1d6 from its saving throws until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. A creature also makes this save when the XPHB moves into its space, when it enters the XPHB, or when it ends its turn inside the XPHB. A creature makes this save only once per turn.\n\nThe XPHB moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns.\n\nCasting as a Circle Spell\n\nCasting this as a Circle spell requires a minimum of five secondary casters. In addition to the spell's usual components, you must provide a special component (a string of three black pearls from Pandemonium), which the spell consumes. The spell's range increases to 1 mile, and its duration increases to until dispelled (no XPHB required). The spell ends early if any caster who participated in this casting contributes to another casting of FRHoF as a Circle spell.\n\nWhen the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 3+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails."},
  ["creature.doomwake-giant.mot2014"]={title="Doomwake Giant",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 162 (13d12 + 78)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 12 | CON 22 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Erebos\n\nAny creature that starts its turn within 10 feet of the giant must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw, or it takes 10 (3d6) necrotic damage and can't regain hit points until the start of its next turn. On a successful saving throw, the creature is immune to the giant's Aura of Erebos for 24 hours.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe giant has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe giant makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (3d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage.\n\nNoxious Gust {@recharge 5}\n\nThe giant exhales a mighty gust that creates a blast of deadly mist in a 60-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) necrotic damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone."},
  ["charoption.doppelganger.idrotf2014"]={title="Doppelganger",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nI'm a shapechanger. I have none of the traits of the race I'm imitating, but I retain my class features, background, and alignment. I have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. I can use an action to do either of the following at will:\n\nI can innately cast detect thoughts, requiring no components. My spellcasting ability is Intelligence. The spell's Wisdom save DC is 8 + my proficiency bonus + my Intelligence modifier. I can polymorph into any humanoid I have seen or back into my true form. My statistics, other than my size, don't change. Any equipment I'm wearing or carrying isn't transformed. I revert to my true form when I die."},
  ["creature.doppelganger.mm2014"]={title="Doppelganger",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe doppelganger can use its action to polymorph into a Small or Medium humanoid it has seen, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nAmbusher\n\nIn the first round of a combat, the doppelganger has advantage on attack rolls against any creature it surprised.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the doppelganger surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe doppelganger makes two melee attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRead Thoughts\n\nThe doppelganger magically reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 60 feet of it. The effect can penetrate barriers, but 3 feet of wood or dirt, 2 feet of stone, 2 inches of metal, or a thin sheet of lead blocks it. While the target is in range, the doppelganger can continue reading its thoughts, as long as the doppelganger's concentration isn't broken (as if concentration on a spell). While reading the target's mind, the doppelganger has advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion) checks against the target."},
  ["creature.doppelganger.xmm2024"]={title="Doppelganger",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 100\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus three other languages\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nRead Thoughts\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe doppelganger makes two Slam attacks and uses Unsettling Visage if available.\n\nSlam\n\nm 6 (with XPHB during the first round of each combat), reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nUnsettling Visage {@recharge}\n\nwis 12, each creature in a 15-foot XPHB originating from the doppelganger that can see the doppelganger. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe doppelganger shape-shifts into a Medium or Small Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.doric.hat-tg2014"]={title="Doric",subtitle="Criatura - HAT-TG - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 16 | WIS 19 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Elvish, Infernal, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDoric makes two Shaped Claw or Sling attacks. She can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nShaped Claw\n\nms 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape (5/Day)\n\nDoric magically transforms into a Beast with a challenge rating of 3 or less or into an owlbear (see the Monster Manual).\n\nDoric can remain in that form for up to 2 hours. She can choose whether her equipment falls to the ground, melds with her new form, or is worn by the new form. Doric reverts to her true form if she is incapacitated or dies. She can revert to her true form using a bonus action.\n\nWhile Doric is transformed, her stat block is replaced by the stat block of that form, except she keeps her current hit points, her hit point maximum, this bonus action, her alignment, and her Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFiery Rebuke (3/Day)\n\nWhen Doric is damaged by a creature that she can see within 60 feet of herself, she magically engulfs the creature in flames. The creature must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) fire damage on failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.doru.cos2014"]={title="Doru",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.double-bladed-scimitar.erlw2014"]={title="Double-Bladed Scimitar",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSpecial\n\nIf you attack with a double-bladed scimitar as part of the Attack action on your turn, you can use a bonus action immediately after to make a melee attack with it. This attack deals 1d4 slashing damage on a hit, instead of 2d4."},
  ["magicitem.dowsing-dagger.xmts2024"]={title="Dowsing Dagger",subtitle="Item Magico - XMtS - 2024",body="Pagina: 19\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nA curved jade blade fashioned by the River Heralds, this +1 dagger can detect the presence of fresh water within 200 feet of the wielder."},
  ["creature.dr-cassee-dannell.kftgv2014"]={title="Dr. Cassee Dannell",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 10"},
  ["magicitem.draakhorn.rot2014"]={title="Draakhorn",subtitle="Item Magico - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThe Draakhorn was a gift from RoT in the war between dragons and giants. It was once the horn of her ancient red dragon consort, Ephelomon, that she gave to dragonkind to help them in their war against the giants. The Draakhorn is a signaling device, and it is so large that it requires two Medium creatures (or one Large or larger) to hold it while a third creature sounds it, making the earth resonate to its call. The horn has been blasted with fire into a dark ebony hue and is wrapped in bands of bronze with draconic runes that glow with purple eldritch fire.\n\nThe low, moaning drone of the Draakhorn discomfits normal animals within a few miles, and it alerts all dragons within two thousand miles to rise and be wary, for great danger is at hand. Coded blasts were once used to signal specific messages. Knowledge of those codes has been lost to the ages.\n\nThose with knowledge of the Draakhorn's history know that it was first built to signal danger to chromatic dragons—a purpose the Cult of the Dragon has corrupted to call chromatic dragons to the Well of Dragons from across the North.\n\nWithin 50 feet of any enclosed space where the horn is blown, the air begins to shimmer from the sound. Any character within 20 feet of the entry to the enclosed space must succeed on a 12 Strength check to continue pushing against the pressure of the sound. A failure indicates the character can advance no farther toward the entry.\n\nFor any character entering the enclosed space, the sound fades to silence—because any creature that enters the enclosed space is temporarily deafened and must make a 12 Constitution saving throw. Success indicates the deafness ends 2 minutes after the Draakhorn ceases to sound. Failure indicates the character remains deafened for 1 hour after the Draakhorn ceases to sound.\n\nWhile the horn is sounding, a creature must make a 15 Constitution saving throw the first time on a turn the creature enters a 150-foot cone in front of the horn or starts its turn there. On a failed save, the creature takes 27 (6d8) thunder damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't knocked prone."},
  ["creature.dracohydra.ftd2014"]={title="Dracohydra",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 176\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 218 (19d12 + 95)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 12 | CON 20 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMultiple Heads\n\nThe dracohydra has five heads. While it has more than one head, the dracohydra has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, and knocked unconscious.\n\nWhenever the dracohydra takes 30 or more damage in a single turn, one of its heads dies. If all its heads die, the dracohydra dies.\n\nAt the end of its turn, the dracohydra grows two heads for each of its heads that died since its last turn, unless it has taken radiant damage since its last turn. The dracohydra regains 10 hit points for each head regrown this way.\n\nReactive Heads\n\nFor each head the dracohydra has beyond one, it gets an extra reaction that can be used only for opportunity attacks.\n\nWakeful\n\nWhile the dracohydra sleeps, at least one of its heads is awake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dracohydra makes as many Bite attacks as it has heads.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) damage of a type chosen by the dracohydra: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison.\n\nPrismatic Breath {@recharge 4}\n\nThe dracohydra's heads exhale a single breath of multicolored energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 33 (6d10) damage of a type chosen by the dracohydra: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage."},
  ["creature.dracolich.xmm2024"]={title="Dracolich",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 102\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H/G\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 225 (18d12 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dracolich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLife Suppression\n\nCreatures within 60 feet of the dracolich can't regain XPHB.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe dracolich has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Gem\n\nThe dracolich has a magical gem. If the dracolich is destroyed while the gem is on the same plane of existence as it, the dracolich gains a new body in 1d20 days, regaining all its XPHB and appearing within 5 feet of the gem.\n\nThe gem is a Tiny object that has AC 20; HP 50; and XPHB to Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The gem regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB. If the gem is destroyed, the dracolich can create a new one by completing an 8-hour ritual using a gem worth 1,000+ GP and by expending 5,000 GP, which the ritual consumes.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dracolich makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 13, reach 10 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nNecrotic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 52 (8d12) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dracolich moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nSickening Ray\n\nThe dracolich uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version). The dracolich can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nTerrifying Presence\n\nwis 19, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the dracolich. actSaveFail 11 (2d10) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dracolich can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.draconian-dreadnought.ftd2014"]={title="Draconian Dreadnought",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 57 (6d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, it bursts into flames and is reduced to ashes. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on the draconian must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 10 (3d6) fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Serrated Sword attacks and one Tail attack.\n\nSerrated Sword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShape Theft\n\nAfter the draconian kills a Medium or smaller Humanoid, the draconian can magically transform itself to look and feel like that creature while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation lasts until the draconian dies or uses an action to end it."},
  ["creature.draconian-foot-soldier.ftd2014"]={title="Draconian Foot Soldier",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 8 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nControlled Fall\n\nWhen the draconian falls and isn't incapacitated, it subtracts up to 100 feet from the fall when calculating the fall's damage.\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, its body turns to stone and releases a petrifying gas. Each creature within 5 feet of the draconian must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be restrained as it begins to turn to stone. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn. On a success, the effect ends; otherwise the creature is petrified for 1 minute. After 1 minute, the body of the draconian crumbles to dust.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Shortsword attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.draconian-infiltrator.ftd2014"]={title="Draconian Infiltrator",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 17 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, it turns into a puddle of acid and splashes acid on those around it. Each creature within 5 feet of the draconian must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or be covered in acid for 1 minute. A creature can use its action to scrape or wash the acid off itself or another creature. A creature covered in the acid takes 7 (2d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nGlide\n\nWhen the draconian falls and isn't incapacitated, it subtracts up to 100 feet from the fall when calculating the fall's damage, and it can move up to 2 feet horizontally for every 1 foot it descends.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Dagger attacks. If both attacks hit the same creature, the target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned until the end of the target's next turn. While poisoned in this way, the target is also paralyzed.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.draconian-mage.ftd2014"]={title="Draconian Mage",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, its scales and flesh immediately shrivel away and its bones explode. Each creature within 10 feet of it must succeed on a 10 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) force damage.\n\nGlide\n\nWhen the draconian falls and isn't incapacitated, it subtracts up to 100 feet from the fall when calculating the fall's damage, and it can move up to 2 feet horizontally for every 1 foot it descends.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Trident or Necrotic Ray attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nNecrotic Ray\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.draconian-mastermind.ftd2014"]={title="Draconian Mastermind",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 35\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 15 | WIS 11 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, its magical essence lashes out as a ball of lightning at the closest creature within 30 feet of it before arcing out to up to two other creatures within 15 feet of the first. Each creature must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 9 (2d8) lightning damage and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't stunned.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes three Rend or Energy Ray attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nEnergy Ray\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) force damage.\n\nNoxious Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe draconian exhales a 15-foot cone of noxious gas. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 21 (6d6) poison damage and gains 1 level of exhaustion. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, doesn't gain exhaustion, and is immune to all draconians' Noxious Breath for 24 hours.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMagic Shield (3/Day)\n\nWhen the draconian is hit by an attack roll, it can create an invisible barrier of magical force around itself, granting it a +5 bonus to its AC against that attack and potentially causing the attack to miss."},
  ["language.draconic.dsotdq2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.draconic.erlw2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["language.draconic.ggr2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.draconic.mot2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.draconic.phb2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\nDraconic is thought to be one of the oldest languages and is often used in the study of magic. The language sounds harsh to most other creatures and includes numerous hard consonants and sibilants."},
  ["language.draconic.psi2014"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - PSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.draconic.xphb2024"]={title="Draconic",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["subclass.draconic-bloodline.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.0"]={title="Draconic Bloodline",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Draconic Bloodline\n\nPagina: 102\n\nYour innate magic comes from draconic magic that was mingled with your blood or that of your ancestors. Most often, sorcerers with this origin trace their descent back to a mighty sorcerer of ancient times who made a bargain with a dragon or who might even have claimed a dragon parent. Some of these bloodlines are well established in the world, but most are obscure. Any given sorcerer could be the first of a new bloodline, as a result of a pact or some other exceptional circumstance.\n\nNivel 1 - Draconic Resilience\n\nPagina: 102\n\nAs magic flows through your body, it causes physical traits of your dragon ancestors to emerge. At 1st level, your hit point maximum increases by 1 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.\n\nAdditionally, parts of your skin are covered by a thin sheen of dragon-like scales. When you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 13 + your Dexterity modifier.\n\nNivel 1 - Draconic Resilience\n\nNivel 1 - Dragon Ancestor\n\nPagina: 102\n\nAt 1st level, you choose one type of dragon as your ancestor. The damage type associated with each dragon is used by features you gain later.\n\nDragon | Damage Type\n\nBlack | spells\n\nBlue | spells\n\nBrass | spells\n\nBronze | spells\n\nCopper | spells\n\nGold | spells\n\nGreen | spells\n\nRed | spells\n\nSilver | spells\n\nWhite | spells\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Draconic. Additionally, whenever you make a Charisma check when interacting with dragons, your proficiency bonus is doubled if it applies to the check.\n\nNivel 1 - Dragon Ancestor\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Bloodline\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Resilience\n\nPagina: 148\n\nThe magic in your body manifests physical traits of your draconic gift. Your XPHB maximum increases by 3, and it increases by 1 whenever you gain another Sorcerer level.\n\nParts of you are also covered by dragon-like scales. While you aren't wearing armor, your base XPHB equals 10 plus your Dexterity and Charisma modifiers.\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Resilience\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Sorcery\n\nPagina: 148\n\nBreathe the Magic of Dragons\n\nYour innate magic comes from the gift of a dragon. Perhaps an ancient dragon facing death bequeathed some of its magical power to you or your ancestor. You might have absorbed magic from a site infused with dragons' power. Or perhaps you handled a treasure taken from a dragon's hoard that was steeped in draconic power. Or you might have a dragon for an ancestor.\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Spells\n\nPagina: 148\n\nWhen you reach a Sorcerer level specified in the Draconic Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nSorcerer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nPagina: 102\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you cast a spell that deals damage of the type associated with your draconic ancestry, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell. At the same time, you can spend 1 sorcery point to gain resistance to that damage type for 1 hour.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nPagina: 148\n\nYour draconic magic has an affinity with a damage type associated with dragons. Choose one of those types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison.\n\nYou have XPHB to that damage type, and when you cast a spell that deals damage of that type, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nPagina: 102\n\nAt 14th level, you gain the ability to sprout a pair of dragon wings from your back, gaining a flying speed equal to your current speed. You can create these wings as a bonus action on your turn. They last until you dismiss them as a bonus action on your turn.\n\nYou can't manifest your wings while wearing armor unless the armor is made to accommodate them, and clothing not made to accommodate your wings might be destroyed when you manifest them.\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nPagina: 148\n\nAs a XPHB, you can cause draconic wings to appear on your back. The wings last for 1 hour or until you dismiss them (no action required). For the duration, you have a XPHB of 60 feet.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you spend 3 Sorcery Points (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nNivel 18 - Draconic Presence\n\nPagina: 102\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you can channel the dread presence of your dragon ancestor, causing those around you to become awestruck or frightened. As an action, you can spend 5 sorcery points to draw on this power and exude an aura of awe or fear (your choice) to a distance of 60 feet. For 1 minute or until you lose your concentration (as if you were casting a concentration spell), each hostile creature that starts its turn in this aura must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed (if you chose awe) or frightened (if you chose fear) until the aura ends. A creature that succeeds on this saving throw is immune to your aura for 24 hours.\n\nNivel 18 - Draconic Presence\n\nNivel 18 - Dragon Companion\n\nPagina: 148\n\nYou can cast XPHB without a Material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require XPHB. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting.\n\nNivel 18 - Dragon Companion"},
  ["feature.draconic-bloodline.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.1"]={title="Draconic Bloodline",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nYour innate magic comes from draconic magic that was mingled with your blood or that of your ancestors. Most often, sorcerers with this origin trace their descent back to a mighty sorcerer of ancient times who made a bargain with a dragon or who might even have claimed a dragon parent. Some of these bloodlines are well established in the world, but most are obscure. Any given sorcerer could be the first of a new bloodline, as a result of a pact or some other exceptional circumstance."},
  ["feature.draconic-bloodline.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.3"]={title="Draconic Bloodline",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.draconic-disciple.ftd2014.monk.ascendant-dragon.3"]={title="Draconic Disciple",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body=""},
  ["reward.draconic-familiar.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Familiar",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYou gain the aid of a draconic familiar, which might be a splinter of the consciousness of a dragon that invested you with power.\n\nYou can cast the find familiar spell as a ritual without using any material components. When you cast the spell in this way, your familiar always takes the form of a pseudodragon.\n\nAdditionally, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of your own attacks to allow your pseudodragon familiar to make one attack of its own with its reaction."},
  ["feature.draconic-gift.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.3"]={title="Draconic Gift",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.draconic-longsword.toa2014"]={title="Draconic Longsword",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis longsword has a dragon-shaped hilt. While you carry it, you gain the ability to speak and understand the Draconic language."},
  ["feature.draconic-presence.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.18"]={title="Draconic Presence",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["reward.draconic-rebirth.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Rebirth",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYou become a dragonborn. You replace the racial traits of your original race with the traits of a chromatic, gem, or metallic dragonborn (detailed in this FTD). The kind of dragonborn you become matches the family of the dragon that is the source of this gift. You can keep any skill proficiencies you gained from your previous race, or you gain proficiency in two skills of your choice."},
  ["feature.draconic-resilience.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.1"]={title="Draconic Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.draconic-resilience.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.3"]={title="Draconic Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["reward.draconic-senses.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Senses",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYou gain keen senses like a dragon's.\n\nBlindsight\n\nYou have blindsight to a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind cover, even if you're blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see invisible creatures within that range, unless the creatures successfully hide from you.\n\nKeen Senses\n\nYou have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks."},
  ["creature.draconic-shard.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Shard",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d12 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 80\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 22 | WIS 18 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, fire\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeflection\n\nThe shard's AC includes its Intelligence modifier.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe shard can move through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. If it ends its turn inside an object, it takes 5 (1d10) force damage.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the shard fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nWhen it drops to 0 hit points, the shard disappears and leaves a Tiny cracked gemstone in its space. The gemstone matches the kind of gem dragon it was in life and has AC 20, 15 hit points, and immunity to all damage except force. Unless the gemstone is destroyed, after 1d20 days, the gemstone dissipates and the shard re-forms, regaining all its hit points and appearing in the place the gemstone once occupied or in the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe shard doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe shard makes two Telekinetic Rend attacks.\n\nTelekinetic Rend\n\nms,rs 12 to hit, reach 10 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) force damage.\n\nInhabit Object\n\nThe shard disappears as it pours its psychic essence into a Medium or smaller nonsentient object it can see within 30 feet of it, magically possessing it. The object uses the shard's AC, and any damage dealt to the object applies to the shard's hit points. The shard inhabits the object until it uses an action to leave; until it is turned; until it is reduced to 0 hit points; or until an effect that ends possession, such as a dispel evil and good spell, is used on it. When it leaves the object, it reappears in the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nWhile inhabited, the object becomes a magic item if it wasn't already, and a Tiny cracked gemstone matching the kind of gem dragon the shard was in life appears somewhere on the object. The shard can cause the object to fly using the shard's own flying speed, use its senses, speak verbally or telepathically, cast spells, and use its legendary actions.\n\nIf a creature wears or carries the inhabited object, the shard can grant the creature the following benefits:\n\nEach of the creature's attacks deals an extra 1d8 force damage on a hit.\n\nThe creature gains resistance to psychic damage.\n\nPsychic Crush {@recharge 5}\n\nThe shard unleashes a pulse of psychic power. Each creature of the shard's choice in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on it must make a 20 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 55 (10d10) psychic damage and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't stunned.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nRend\n\nThe shard makes one Telekinetic Rend attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe shard uses Spellcasting.\n\nCommanding Thought (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe shard targets a creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 20 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed until the end of its next turn. While charmed in this way, the target becomes the shard's puppet, acting and moving in accordance with its telepathic commands. While under the shard's control, the target can take only the Attack (shard chooses the target) or Dash action on its turn."},
