enever you gain another Sorcerer level.\n\nParts of you are also covered by dragon-like scales. While you aren't wearing armor, your base XPHB equals 10 plus your Dexterity and Charisma modifiers.\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Resilience\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Sorcery\n\nPagina: 148\n\nBreathe the Magic of Dragons\n\nYour innate magic comes from the gift of a dragon. Perhaps an ancient dragon facing death bequeathed some of its magical power to you or your ancestor. You might have absorbed magic from a site infused with dragons' power. Or perhaps you handled a treasure taken from a dragon's hoard that was steeped in draconic power. Or you might have a dragon for an ancestor.\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Spells\n\nPagina: 148\n\nWhen you reach a Sorcerer level specified in the Draconic Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nSorcerer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nPagina: 102\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you cast a spell that deals damage of the type associated with your draconic ancestry, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell. At the same time, you can spend 1 sorcery point to gain resistance to that damage type for 1 hour.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nPagina: 148\n\nYour draconic magic has an affinity with a damage type associated with dragons. Choose one of those types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison.\n\nYou have XPHB to that damage type, and when you cast a spell that deals damage of that type, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Affinity\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nPagina: 102\n\nAt 14th level, you gain the ability to sprout a pair of dragon wings from your back, gaining a flying speed equal to your current speed. You can create these wings as a bonus action on your turn. They last until you dismiss them as a bonus action on your turn.\n\nYou can't manifest your wings while wearing armor unless the armor is made to accommodate them, and clothing not made to accommodate your wings might be destroyed when you manifest them.\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nPagina: 148\n\nAs a XPHB, you can cause draconic wings to appear on your back. The wings last for 1 hour or until you dismiss them (no action required). For the duration, you have a XPHB of 60 feet.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you spend 3 Sorcery Points (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nNivel 14 - Dragon Wings\n\nNivel 18 - Draconic Presence\n\nPagina: 102\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you can channel the dread presence of your dragon ancestor, causing those around you to become awestruck or frightened. As an action, you can spend 5 sorcery points to draw on this power and exude an aura of awe or fear (your choice) to a distance of 60 feet. For 1 minute or until you lose your concentration (as if you were casting a concentration spell), each hostile creature that starts its turn in this aura must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed (if you chose awe) or frightened (if you chose fear) until the aura ends. A creature that succeeds on this saving throw is immune to your aura for 24 hours.\n\nNivel 18 - Draconic Presence\n\nNivel 18 - Dragon Companion\n\nPagina: 148\n\nYou can cast XPHB without a Material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require XPHB. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting.\n\nNivel 18 - Dragon Companion"},
  ["feature.draconic-sorcery.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.3"]={title="Draconic Sorcery",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 148\n\nBreathe the Magic of Dragons\n\nYour innate magic comes from the gift of a dragon. Perhaps an ancient dragon facing death bequeathed some of its magical power to you or your ancestor. You might have absorbed magic from a site infused with dragons' power. Or perhaps you handled a treasure taken from a dragon's hoard that was steeped in draconic power. Or you might have a dragon for an ancestor."},
  ["feature.draconic-spells.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.3"]={title="Draconic Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 148\n\nWhen you reach a Sorcerer level specified in the Draconic Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nSorcerer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.draconic-spirit.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, understands the languages you speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShared Resistances\n\nWhen you summon the dragon, choose one of its damage resistances. You have resistance to the chosen damage type until the spell ends.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes a number of Rend attacks equal to half the spell's level (rounded down), and it uses Breath Weapon.\n\nRend\n\nmw your spell attack modifier to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h1d6 + 4 + summonSpellLevel piercing damage.\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nThe dragon exhales destructive energy in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC. A creature takes 2d6 damage of a type this dragon has resistance to (your choice) on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.draconic-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Draconic Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 325\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, understands the languages you know\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShared Resistances\n\nWhen you summon the spirit, choose one of its Resistances. You have XPHB to the chosen damage type until the spell ends.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spirit makes a number of Rend attacks equal to half the spell's level (round down), and it uses Breath Weapon.\n\nRend\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 10 feet. h1d6 + 4 + summonSpellLevel Piercing damage.\n\nBreath Weapon\n\ndex DC equals your spell save DC, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 2d6 damage of a type this spirit has XPHB to (your choice when you cast the spell). actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["spell.draconic-transformation.ftd2014"]={title="Draconic Transformation",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 7 - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nWith a roar, you draw on the magic of dragons to transform yourself, taking on draconic features. You gain the following benefits until the spell ends:\n\n• Blindsight You have blindsight with a range of 30 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind Cover, even if you're blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an invisible creature, unless the creature successfully hides from you.\n\n• Breath Weapon When you cast this spell, and as a bonus action on subsequent turns for the duration, you can exhale shimmering energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 6d8 force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• Wings Incorporeal wings sprout from your back, giving you a flying speed of 60 feet."},
  ["creature.dracophage-subject.dsotdq2014"]={title="Dracophage Subject",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be infected with a disease—a minuscule slaad egg.\n\nA Humanoid host can carry only one slaad egg at a time. Over three months, the egg moves to the chest cavity, gestates, and forms a slaad tadpole. In the 24-hour period before the tadpole is born, the host feels unwell; its speed is halved; and it has disadvantage on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws. At birth, the tadpole chews its way through vital organs and out of the host's chest in 1 round, killing the host in the process.\n\nIf the disease is cured before the tadpole's emergence, the tadpole disintegrates."},
  ["creature.draegloth.mpmm2014"]={title="Draegloth",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 11 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe draegloth has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put it to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draegloth makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.draegloth.vgm2014"]={title="Draegloth",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 11 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe draegloth has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put it to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draegloth makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.draft-horse.mm2014"]={title="Draft Horse",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 321\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 19 (3d10 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.draft-horse.phb2014"]={title="Draft Horse",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.draft-horse.xmm2024"]={title="Draft Horse",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 352\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.draft-horse.xphb2024"]={title="Draft Horse",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.dragon.psk2014"]={title="Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.dragon.tce2014.druid.stars.2"]={title="Dragon",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nA constellation of a wise dragon appears on you. When you make an Intelligence or a Wisdom check or a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration on a spell, you can treat a roll of 9 or lower on the d20 as a 10."},
  ["item.dragon.wdh2014"]={title="Dragon",subtitle="Item - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nRaridade: none\n\nGold coin, half again as large as a wdh (1 dragon = 100 wdh)"},
  ["feature.dragon.xphb2024.druid.stars.3"]={title="Dragon",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.dragon-ancestor.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.1"]={title="Dragon Ancestor",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.dragon-army-dragonnel.dsotdq2014"]={title="Dragon Army Dragonnel",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 58 (9d10 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Draconic but can't speak\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragonnel doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonnel makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) fire damage."},
  ["creature.dragon-army-officer.dsotdq2014"]={title="Dragon Army Officer",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDraconic Devotion\n\nWhile the officer can see a Dragon that isn't hostile to it, the officer has advantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe officer makes two Vicious Lance attacks and uses Assault Orders if it's available.\n\nVicious Lance\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) fire damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) fire damage.\n\nAssault Orders {@recharge 5}\n\nThe officer shouts orders and targets up to two other creatures within 60 feet of itself. If a target has the Draconic Devotion trait and can hear the officer, the target can use its reaction to make one melee attack."},
  ["creature.dragon-army-soldier.dsotdq2014"]={title="Dragon Army Soldier",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDraconic Devotion\n\nWhile the soldier can see a Dragon that isn't hostile to it, the soldier has advantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe soldier makes two Longsword or Javelin attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands, plus 2 (1d4) fire damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) fire damage."},
  ["creature.dragon-blessed.ftd2014"]={title="Dragon Blessed",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 17 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, and any two languages\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blessed makes two Mace or Radiant Bolt attacks.\n\nMace\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) radiant damage.\n\nRadiant Bolt\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h22 (5d8) radiant damage, and the blessed regains 5 (1d10) hit points."},
  ["creature.dragon-chosen.ftd2014"]={title="Dragon Chosen",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe chosen makes one Handaxe attack and two Shortsword attacks.\n\nHandaxe\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage. homThe handaxe magically returns to the chosen's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nBiting Rebuke\n\nImmediately after the chosen takes damage from a creature within 5 feet of it, it can make a Shortsword attack with advantage against that creature."},
  ["feature.dragon-companion.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.18"]={title="Dragon Companion",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["background.dragon-cultist.frhof2014"]={title="Dragon Cultist",subtitle="Background - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["feat.dragon-fear.xge2024"]={title="Dragon Fear",subtitle="Feat - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen angered, you radiate menace. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• Instead of exhaling destructive energy, you can expend a use of your Breath Weapon trait to roar, forcing each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you to make a Wisdom saving throw (8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier). A target automatically succeeds on the save if it can't hear or see you. On a failed save, a target becomes frightened of you for 1 minute. If the frightened target takes any damage, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["feat.dragon-hide.xge2024"]={title="Dragon Hide",subtitle="Feat - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 74\n\nYou manifest scales and claws reminiscent of your draconic ancestors. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• Your scales harden. While you aren't wearing armor, you can calculate your AC as 13 + your Dexterity modifier. You can use a shield and still gain this benefit.\n\n• You grow retractable claws from the tips of your fingers. Extending or retracting the claws requires no action. The claws are natural weapons, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier, instead of the normal bludgeoning damage for an unarmed strike."},
  ["creature.dragon-hunter.jttrc2014"]={title="Dragon Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 138\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 13"},
  ["reward.dragon-queen-s-will.dsotdq2014"]={title="Dragon Queen's Will",subtitle="Recompensa - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\nYou've seen a glimpse of the Dragon Queen's ambitions. It haunts your dreams but steels your will to oppose her. This charm grants you a +4 bonus on Wisdom saving throws. Once used three times, the charm vanishes. While you have this charm, you suffer unsettling but harmless dreams of ravenous dragons. You also permanently gain the ability to speak Draconic if you couldn't already."},
  ["charoption.dragon-scholar.hotdq2014"]={title="Dragon Scholar",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\nYou have studied dragons and their lore for many years. You can automatically identify locations built or used by dragons and can identify dragon eggs and scales by sight. If you fail an Intelligence check to recall lore relating to dragons, you know someone or some book you can consult for the answer unless the DM rules that the lore is unknown."},
  ["magicitem.dragon-sensing-longsword.pota2014"]={title="Dragon Sensing Longsword",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis +1 longsword is made of dragon bone and with a dragon-leather grip. It has rubies in its pommel and hilt. The sword grows warm and the rubies glow slightly when the sword is within 120 feet of a dragon."},
  ["creature.dragon-speaker.ftd2014"]={title="Dragon Speaker",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 36 (8d6 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 11 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, and any two languages\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe speaker makes two Thunder Bolt attacks.\n\nThunder Bolt\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h13 (3d8) thunder damage, and the target is pushed horizontally up to 10 feet away from the speaker.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDisarming Words (3/Day)\n\nWhen a creature the speaker can see within 60 feet of it makes a damage roll, the speaker can roll a d6 and subtract the number rolled from that damage roll."},
  ["magicitem.dragon-thighbone-club.skt2014"]={title="Dragon Thighbone Club",subtitle="Item Magico - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nThis red dragon's thighbone is 14 feet long, 250 lbs, and is wrapped in old leather, suggesting that it was once used as a giant's greatclub.\n\nWhen you hit a creature of the dragon type with this weapon, it deals an extra 2d8 bludgeoning damage.\n\nIf you attune to the greatclub, it magically shrinks to a size that you can wield effectively."},
  ["creature.dragon-tortoise.cm2014"]={title="Dragon Tortoise",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Terran"},
  ["creature.dragon-turtle.mm2014"]={title="Dragon Turtle",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 341 (22d20 + 110)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon turtle can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon turtle makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws. It can make one tail attack in place of its two claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h26 (3d12 + 7) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h26 (3d12 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 20 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away from the dragon turtle and knocked prone.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon turtle exhales scalding steam in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 52 (15d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Being underwater doesn't grant resistance against this damage."},
  ["creature.dragon-turtle.xmm2024"]={title="Dragon Turtle",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 103\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 356 (23d20 + 115)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 50\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Primordial (Aquan)\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Bite attacks. It can replace one attack with a Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nm 13, reach 15 ft. h23 (3d10 + 7) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage. Being underwater doesn't grant XPHB to this Fire damage.\n\nTail\n\nm 13, reach 15 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 19, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 56 (16d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail Being underwater doesn't grant XPHB to this Fire damage."},
  ["creature.dragon-turtle-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Dragon Turtle Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon turtle can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (1d12 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon turtle exhales steam in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Being underwater doesn't grant resistance against this damage."},
  ["feature.dragon-wings.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.14"]={title="Dragon Wings",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.dragon-wings.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.14"]={title="Dragon Wings",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.dragon-s-blood.erlw2014"]={title="Dragon's Blood",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\nRaridade: none\n\nIntroduced into Sharn by Daask, dragon's blood is a potent and highly addictive stimulant. In addition to inducing euphoria, it can enhance spellcasting ability or even temporarily imbue a user with the ability to cast sorcerer spells. The drug's effects are potentially dangerous and always unpredictable. This isn't something a player character should want to use; adventurers are more likely to interfere with Daask smugglers or deal with an addict who accidentally casts a fireball in a crowded street. The specific effects of dragon's blood are up to you, but you can take inspiration from the PHB table in the PHB."},
  ["spell.dragon-s-breath.xge2024"]={title="Dragon's Breath",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 154\n\nYou touch one willing creature and imbue it with the power to spew magical energy from its mouth, provided it has one. Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. Until the spell ends, the creature can use an action to exhale energy of the chosen type in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 damage of the chosen type on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["spell.dragon-s-breath.xphb2024"]={title="Dragon's Breath",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 266\n\nYou touch one willing creature, and choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison. Until the spell ends, the target can take a XPHB action to exhale a 15-foot XPHB. Each creature in that area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 damage of the chosen type on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.dragonbait.toa2014"]={title="Dragonbait",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: disease\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDivine Health\n\nDragonbait is immune to disease.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nWhile holding his holy avenger longsword, Dragonbait creates an aura in a 10-foot radius around him. While this aura is active, Dragonbait and all creatures friendly to him in the aura have advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDragonbait makes two melee weapon attacks.\n\nHoly Avenger (+3 Longsword)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage, or 10 (1d10 + 5) slashing damage when used with two hands. If the target is a fiend or an undead it takes an extra 11 (2d10) radiant damage.\n\nSense Alignment\n\nDragonbait chooses one creature he can see within 60 feet of him and determines its alignment, as long as the creature isn't hidden from divination magic by a spell or other magical effect."},
  ["creature.dragonblood-ooze.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonblood Ooze",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 6 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic and the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe ooze can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe ooze can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ooze makes two Pseudopod attacks. The ooze can replace one Pseudopod attack with its Slime Breath, if available.\n\nPseudopod\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) acid damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 15). Until this grapple ends, the target takes 7 (2d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nSlime Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe ooze expels a spray of its gelatinous mass in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) acid damage and is pulled up to 30 feet straight toward the ooze. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pulled."},
  ["creature.dragonbone-golem.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonbone Golem",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 161 (19d10 + 57)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic and the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nEach creature of the golem's choice that starts its turn within 20 feet of the golem must make a 15 Wisdom saving throw unless the golem is incapacitated. On a failed save, the creature is frightened until the start of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature is immune to this golem's Fear Aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe golem doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes one Pinion attack and two Rend attacks.\n\nPinion\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is pinned beneath the bony pinion and restrained. The golem has two pinions, each of which can restrain one target. If a creature is restrained by one of the pinions, the golem can't attack with it. Any creature restrained by a pinion can free itself at the start of its turn with a successful 17 Strength (Athletics) check.\n\nRend\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) necrotic damage.\n\nPetrifying Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe golem emits a 60-foot cone of petrifying gas from its mouth. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or take 35 (10d6) poison damage and be restrained as it begins to turn to stone. The restrained target must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the effect ends on the target. On a failed save, the target is petrified."},
  ["species.dragonborn.phb2014"]={title="Dragonborn",subtitle="Especie - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nAge\n\nYoung dragonborn grow quickly. They walk hours after hatching, attain the size and development of a 10-year-old human child by the age of 3, and reach adulthood by 15. They live to be around 80.\n\nSize\n\nDragonborn are taller and heavier than humans, standing well over 6 feet tall and averaging almost 250 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nDraconic Ancestry\n\nYou have draconic ancestry. Choose one type of dragon from the Draconic Ancestry table. Your breath weapon and damage resistance are determined by the dragon type, as shown in the table.\n\nDragon | Damage Type | Breath Weapon\n\nBlack | Acid | 5 by 30 ft. line (Dex. save)\n\nBlue | Lightning | 5 by 30 ft. line (Dex. save)\n\nBrass | Fire | 5 by 30 ft. line (Dex. save)\n\nBronze | Lightning | 5 by 30 ft. line (Dex. save)\n\nCopper | Acid | 5 by 30 ft. line (Dex. save)\n\nGold | Fire | 15 ft. cone (Dex. save)\n\nGreen | Poison | 15 ft. cone (Con. save)\n\nRed | Fire | 15 ft. cone (Dex. save)\n\nSilver | Cold | 15 ft. cone (Con. save)\n\nWhite | Cold | 15 ft. cone (Con. save)\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nYou can use your action to exhale destructive energy. Your draconic ancestry determines the size, shape, and damage type of the exhalation.\n\nWhen you use your breath weapon, each creature in the area of the exhalation must make a saving throw, the type of which is determined by your draconic ancestry. The DC for this saving throw equals 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus. A creature takes 2d6 damage on a failed save, and half as much damage on a successful one. The damage increases to 3d6 at 6th level, 4d6 at 11th level, and 5d6 at 16th level.\n\nAfter you use your breath weapon, you can't use it again until you complete a short or long rest.\n\nDamage Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Draconic. Draconic is thought to be one of the oldest languages and is often used in the study of magic. The language sounds harsh to most other creatures and includes numerous hard consonants and sibilants."},
  ["species.dragonborn.xphb2024"]={title="Dragonborn",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 187\n\nDraconic Ancestry\n\nYour lineage stems from a dragon progenitor. Choose the kind of dragon from the Draconic Ancestors table. Your choice affects your Breath Weapon and XPHB XPHB traits as well as your appearance.\n\nDragon | Damage Type\n\nBlack | Acid\n\nBlue | Lightning\n\nBrass | Fire\n\nBronze | Lightning\n\nCopper | Acid\n\nGold | Fire\n\nGreen | Poison\n\nRed | Fire\n\nSilver | Cold\n\nWhite | Cold\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation of magical energy in either a 15-foot XPHB or a 30-foot XPHB that is 5 feet wide (choose the shape each time). Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw (8 plus your Constitution modifier and XPHB). On a failed save, a creature takes 1d10 damage of the type determined by your Draconic Ancestry trait. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach character levels 5 (2d10), 11 (3d10), and 17 (4d10).\n\nYou can use this Breath Weapon a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nDamage Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB to the damage type determined by your Draconic Ancestry trait.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nDraconic Flight\n\nWhen you reach character level 5, you can channel draconic magic to give yourself temporary flight. As a XPHB, you sprout spectral wings on your back that last for 10 minutes or until you retract the wings (no action required) or have the XPHB condition. During that time, you have a XPHB equal to your XPHB. Your wings appear to be made of the same energy as your Breath Weapon. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["species.dragonborn-chromatic.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn (Chromatic)",subtitle="Especie - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nChromatic Ancestry\n\nYou have a chromatic dragon ancestor, granting you a special magical affinity. Choose one kind of dragon from the Chromatic Ancestry table. This determines the damage type for your other traits, as shown in the table.\n\nDragon | Damage Type\n\nBlack | Acid\n\nBlue | Lightning\n\nGreen | Poison\n\nRed | Fire\n\nWhite | Cold\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nWhen you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation of magical energy in a 30-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC = 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus). On a failed save, the creature takes 1d10 damage of the type associated with your Chromatic Ancestry. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10).\n\nYou can use your Breath Weapon a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nDraconic Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to the damage type associated with your Chromatic Ancestry.\n\nChromatic Warding\n\nStarting at 5th level, as an action, you can channel your draconic energy to protect yourself. For 1 minute, you become immune to the damage type associated with your Chromatic Ancestry. Once you use this trait, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["species.dragonborn-gem.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn (Gem)",subtitle="Especie - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nGem Ancestry\n\nYou have a gem dragon ancestor, granting you a special magical affinity. Choose one kind of dragon from the Gem Ancestry table. This determines the damage type for your other traits, as shown in the table.\n\nDragon | Damage Type\n\nAmethyst | Force\n\nCrystal | Radiant\n\nEmerald | Psychic\n\nSapphire | Thunder\n\nTopaz | Necrotic\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nWhen you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation of magical energy in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC = 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus). On a failed save, the creature takes 1d10 damage of the type associated with your Gem Ancestry. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10).\n\nYou can use your Breath Weapon a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nDraconic Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to the damage type associated with your Gem Ancestry.\n\nPsionic Mind\n\nYou can send telepathic messages to any creature you can see within 30 feet of you. You don't need to share a language with the creature for it to understand these messages, but it must be able to understand at least one language to comprehend them.\n\nGem Flight\n\nStarting at 5th level, you can use a bonus action to manifest spectral wings on your body. These wings last for 1 minute. For the duration, you gain a flying speed equal to your walking speed and can hover. Once you use this trait, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["species.dragonborn-metallic.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn (Metallic)",subtitle="Especie - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nMetallic Ancestry\n\nYou have a metallic dragon ancestor, granting you a special magical affinity. Choose one kind of dragon from the Metallic Ancestry table. This determines the damage type for your other traits, as shown in the table.\n\nDragon | Damage Type\n\nBrass | Fire\n\nBronze | Lightning\n\nCopper | Acid\n\nGold | Fire\n\nSilver | Cold\n\nBreath Weapon\n\nWhen you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation of magical energy in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC = 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus). On a failed save, the creature takes 1d10 damage of the type associated with your Metallic Ancestry. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10).\n\nYou can use your Breath Weapon a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nDraconic Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to the damage type associated with your Metallic Ancestry.\n\nMetallic Breath Weapon\n\nAt 5th level, you gain a second breath weapon. When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation in a 15-foot cone. The save DC for this breath is 8 + your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus. Whenever you use this trait, choose one:\n\n• Enervating Breath Each creature in the cone must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or become incapacitated until the start of your next turn.\n\n• Repulsion Breath Each creature in the cone must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed 20 feet away from you and be knocked prone.\n\nOnce you use your Metallic Breath Weapon, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.dragonborn-of-bahamut.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn of Bahamut",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (1/Day)\n\nIf the dragonborn fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonborn makes three Longsword attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands, plus 13 (3d8) radiant damage. The dragonborn can cause the sword to flare with bright light, and the target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the start of the dragonborn's next turn. The sword can flare in this way only once per turn.\n\nHealing Touch (1/Day)\n\nThe dragonborn touches another creature within 5 feet of it. The target magically regains 40 hit points. In addition, all diseases and poisons affecting the target are removed.\n\nRadiant Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe dragonborn exhales fiery radiance in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 44 (8d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. When the dragonborn uses this action, it can choose up to three creatures in the cone. These creatures take no damage from the radiance and instead regain 22 (4d10) hit points each."},
  ["creature.dragonborn-of-sardior.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn of Sardior",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 18 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (1/Day)\n\nIf the dragonborn fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMental Defense\n\nWhile the dragonborn is wearing no armor, its AC includes its Intelligence modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonborn makes three Mind Blade attacks.\n\nMind Blade\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nHeat Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe dragonborn exhales a wave of intense heat in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Metal objects in that area glow red-hot until the end of the dragonborn's next turn. Any creature in physical contact with a heated object at the start of its turn must make a 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 9 (2d8) fire damage and has disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.dragonborn-of-tiamat.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonborn of Tiamat",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 85 (10d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (1/Day)\n\nIf the dragonborn fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonborn makes two Greataxe attacks.\n\nGreataxe\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (1d12 + 5) slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) necrotic damage.\n\nNecrotic Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe dragonborn exhales shadowy fire in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) necrotic damage and is frightened of the dragonborn for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't frightened. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["item.dragonchess-set.phb2014"]={title="Dragonchess Set",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.dragonchess-set.xphb2024"]={title="Dragonchess Set",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Wisdom\n\n• Utilize: Discern whether someone is cheating (10), or win the game (20)"},
  ["creature.dragonclaw.hotdq2014"]={title="Dragonclaw",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDragon Fanatic\n\nThe dragonclaw has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. While the dragonclaw can see a dragon or higher-ranking Cult of the Dragon cultist friendly to it, the dragonclaw ignores the effects of being charmed or frightened.\n\nFanatic Advantage\n\nOnce per turn, if the dragonclaw makes a weapon attack with advantage on the attack roll and hits, it deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe dragonclaw has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the dragonclaw's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonclaw attacks twice with its scimitar.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.dragonfang.rot2014"]={title="Dragonfang",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDragon Fanatic\n\nThe dragonfang has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. While the dragonfang can see a dragon or higher-ranking Cult of the Dragon cultist friendly to it, the dragonfang ignores the effects of being charmed or frightened.\n\nFanatic Advantage\n\nOnce per turn, if the dragonfang makes a weapon attack with advantage on the attack roll and hits, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) damage.\n\nLimited Flight\n\nThe dragonfang can use a bonus action to gain a flying speed of 30 feet until the end of its turn.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe dragonfang has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the dragonfang's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Dragonfang attacks twice with its shortsword.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) damage of the type to which the dragonfang has resistance.\n\nOrb of Dragon's Breath (2/Day)\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 50 ft., one target. h22 (5d8) damage of the type to which the dragonfang has damage resistance."},
  ["creature.dragonflesh-abomination.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonflesh Abomination",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 66 (7d12 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Draconic but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCloying Miasma\n\nThe abomination is surrounded by a noxious stench. At the start of the abomination's turn, any creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of the abomination's next turn.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe abomination regains 10 hit points at the start of its turns if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abomination makes three attacks using Claw, Acidic Spit, or a combination of them. It can replace one of the attacks with a Tail attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) poison damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nAcidic Spit\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) acid damage.\n\nAcid Belch {@recharge 5}\n\nThe abomination belches forth a cloud of acidic gas in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.dragonflesh-grafter.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonflesh Grafter",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grafter makes one Claw attack and one Greatclub attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) poison damage.\n\nGreatclub\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nAcid Retch {@recharge 5}\n\nThe grafter retches forth a spray of acidic bile in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["magicitem.dragongleam.hotdq2014"]={title="Dragongleam",subtitle="Item Magico - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis spear is enchanted with 10 charges of a daylight spell for use in twilight or dark forest underbrush. The command phrase is \"Tiamat's eyes shine,\" written in Draconic runes on the spear's crossguard."},
  ["magicitem.dragonguard.lmop2014"]={title="Dragonguard",subtitle="Item Magico - LMoP - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to AC while wearing this armor.\n\nThis +1 breastplate has a gold dragon motif worked into its design. Created for a human hero of Neverwinter named Tergon, it grants its wearer advantage on saving throws against the breath weapons of creatures that have the dragon type."},
  ["magicitem.dragonguard.pabtso2014"]={title="Dragonguard",subtitle="Item Magico - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to AC while wearing this armor.\n\nThis breastplate has a gold dragon motif worked into its design. Created for a human hero of old Neverwinter named Tergon, it grants its wearer advantage on saving throws against the breath weapons of Dragons.\n\nThis armor consists of a fitted metal chest piece worn with supple leather. Although it leaves the legs and arms relatively unprotected, this armor provides good protection for the wearer's vital organs while leaving the wearer relatively unencumbered."},
  ["creature.dragonnel.ftd2014"]={title="Dragonnel",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 58 (9d10 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic and Common but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragonnel doesn't provoke an opportunity attack when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonnel makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.dragonpriest.tftyp2014"]={title="Dragonpriest",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 5\n\nPV: 30 (8d10 + 40)\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Draconic"},
  ["feat.dragonscarred.frhof2014"]={title="Dragonscarred",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nDamage Resistance\n\nWhen you gain this feat, choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison. You have XPHB to the chosen damage type.\n\nFearsome Power\n\nWhen you deal damage to a creature as part of the XPHB or XPHB action on your turn, you can use the Dragon's Terror benefit of the Cult of the Dragon Initiate feat as a XPHB this turn."},
  ["creature.dragonsoul.rot2014"]={title="Dragonsoul",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 110 (17d8 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDragon Fanatic\n\nThe dragonsoul has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. While the dragonsoul can see a dragon or higher-ranking Cult of the Dragon cultist friendly to it, the dragonsoul ignores the effects of being charmed or frightened.\n\nFanatic Advantage\n\nOnce per turn, if the dragonsoul makes a weapon attack with advantage on the attack roll and hits, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) damage.\n\nLimited Flight\n\nThe dragonsoul can use a bonus action to gain a flying speed of 30 feet until the end of its turn.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe dragonsoul has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the dragonsoul's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Dragonsoul attacks twice with its shortsword.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) damage of the type to which the dragonsoul has resistance.\n\nOrb of Dragon's Breath (3/Day)\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 90 ft., one target. h27 (6d8) damage of the type to which the dragonsoul has damage resistance."},
  ["magicitem.dragonstaff-of-ahghairon.wdh2014"]={title="Dragonstaff of Ahghairon",subtitle="Item Magico - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhile holding the dragonstaff of Ahghairon, you have advantage on saving throws against the spells and breath weapons of dragons, as well as the breath weapons of other creatures of the dragon type (such as dragon turtles).\n\nA creature of the dragon type that you touch with the staff can move through the city of Waterdeep, ignoring Ahghairon's dragonward (see \"Ahghairon's Dragonward,\" in the Introduction). This effect lasts until the creature is touched again by the staff or until a time you proclaim when you confer the benefit.\n\nThe staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge as an action to cast the command spell. If you target a dragon with this casting, the dragon has disadvantage on its saving throw. The staff regains 1d10 charges daily at dawn."},
  ["magicitem.dragontooth-dagger.rot2014"]={title="Dragontooth Dagger",subtitle="Item Magico - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA dagger fashioned from the tooth of a dragon. While the blade is obviously a fang or predator's tooth, the handle is leather wrapped around the root of the tooth, and there is no crossguard.\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this weapon. On a hit with this weapon, the target takes an extra 1d6 acid damage.\n\nDraconic Potency\n\nAgainst enemies of the Cult of the Dragon, the dagger's bonus to attack and damage rolls increases to 2, and the extra acid damage increases to 2d6."},
  ["creature.dragonwing.hotdq2014"]={title="Dragonwing",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDragon Fanatic\n\nThe dragonwing has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. While the dragonwing can see a dragon or higher-ranking Cult of the Dragon cultist friendly to it, the dragonwing ignores the effects of being charmed or frightened.\n\nFanatic Advantage\n\nOnce per turn, if the dragonwing makes a weapon attack with advantage on the attack roll and hits, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage.\n\nLimited Flight\n\nThe dragonwing can use a bonus action to gain a flying speed of 30 feet until the end of its turn.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe dragonwing has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the dragonwing's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonwing attacks twice with its scimitar.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) damage of the type to which the cultist has resistance."},
  ["creature.drake-large.psk2014"]={title="Drake (Large)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.drake-large.psz2014"]={title="Drake (Large)",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.drake-small.psk2014"]={title="Drake (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.drake-small.psz2014"]={title="Drake (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.drake-companion.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.3"]={title="Drake Companion",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.drake-companion.ftd2014"]={title="Drake Companion",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / S\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDraconic Essence\n\nWhen you summon the drake, choose a damage type: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. The chosen type determines the drake's damage immunity and the damage of its Infused Strikes trait.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 plus PB to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d6 plus PB piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nInfused Strikes\n\nWhen another creature within 30 feet of the drake that it can see hits a target with a weapon attack, the drake infuses the strike with its essence, causing the target to take an extra 1d6 damage of the type determined by its Draconic Essence."},
  ["feature.drake-s-breath.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.11"]={title="Drake's Breath",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n11th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nAs an action, you can exhale a 30-foot cone of damaging breath or cause your drake to exhale it. Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice doesn't have to match your drake's Draconic Essence). Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nThis damage increases to 10d6 when you reach 15th level in this class.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use it again."},
  ["subclass.drakewarden.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.0"]={title="Drakewarden",subtitle="Subclasse - FTD - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Gift\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Drakewarden feature\n\nThe bond you share with your drake creates a connection to dragonkind, granting you understanding and empowering your presence. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• Thaumaturgy\n\n• Tongue of Dragons\n\nNivel 3 - Draconic Gift\n\nNivel 3 - Drake Companion\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Drakewarden feature\n\nAs an action, you can magically summon the drake that is bound to you. It appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of you.\n\nThe drake is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See its game statistics in the accompanying FTD stat block, which uses your proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. Whenever you summon the drake, choose a damage type listed in its Draconic Essence trait. You can determine the cosmetic characteristics of the drake, such as its color, its scale texture, or any visible effect of its Draconic Essence; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.\n\nIn combat, the drake shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It can move and use its reaction on its own, but the only action it takes on its turn is the Dodge action, unless you take a bonus action on your turn to command it to take another action. That action can be one in its stat block or some other action. If you are incapacitated, the drake can take any action of its choice, not just Dodge.\n\nThe drake remains until it is reduced to 0 hit points, until you use this feature to summon the drake again, or until you die. Anything the drake was wearing or carrying is left behind when the drake vanishes.\n\nOnce you summon the drake, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher to summon it.\n\nNivel 3 - Drake Companion\n\nNivel 3 - Drakewarden\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYour connection to the natural world takes the form of a draconic spirit, which can manifest in physical form as a drake. As your powers grow, your drake grows as well, blossoming from a small four-legged companion to a majestic winged creature large and strong enough for you to ride. Along the way, you gain an increasing share of the awe-inspiring power of dragons.\n\nConsider the source of the draconic spirit you have bonded with. The Drakewarden Origin table offers examples.\n\nd6 | Origin\n\n1 | You studied a dragon's scale or claw, or a trinket from a dragon's hoard, creating your bond through that token's lingering draconic magic.\n\n2 | A secret order of rangers who collect and guard draconic lore taught you their ways.\n\n3 | A dragon gave you a geode or gemstone to care for. To your surprise, the drake hatched from that stone.\n\n4 | You ingested a few drops of dragon blood, forever infusing your nature magic with draconic power.\n\n5 | An ancient Draconic inscription on a standing stone empowered you when you read it aloud.\n\n6 | You had a vivid dream of a mysterious figure accompanied by seven yellow canaries, who warned you of impending doom. When you awoke, your drake was there, watching you.\n\nNivel 7 - Bond of Fang and Scale\n\nPagina: 15\n\n7th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nThe bond you share with your drake intensifies, protecting you and stoking the drake's fury. When you summon your drake, it grows wings on its back and gains a flying speed equal to its walking speed.\n\nIn addition, while your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:\n\n• Drake Mount The drake grows to Medium size. Reflecting your special bond, you can use the drake as a mount if your size is Medium or smaller. While you are riding your drake, it can't use the flying speed of this feature.\n\n• Magic Fang The drake's Bite attack deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence.\n\n• Resistance You gain resistance to the damage type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence.\n\nNivel 11 - Drake's Breath\n\nPagina: 15\n\n11th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nAs an action, you can exhale a 30-foot cone of damaging breath or cause your drake to exhale it. Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice doesn't have to match your drake's Draconic Essence). Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nThis damage increases to 10d6 when you reach 15th level in this class.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use it again.\n\nNivel 15 - Perfected Bond\n\nPagina: 15\n\n15th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nYour bond to your drake reaches the pinnacle of its power. While your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:\n\n• Empowered Bite The drake's Bite attack deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for its Draconic Essence (for a total of 2d6 extra damage).\n\n• Large Drake The drake grows to Large size. When you ride your drake, it is no longer prohibited from using the flying speed of Bond of Fang and Scale.\n\n• Reflexive Resistance When either you or the drake takes damage while you're within 30 feet of each other, you can use your reaction to give yourself or the drake resistance to that instance of damage. You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.drakewarden.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.3"]={title="Drakewarden",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYour connection to the natural world takes the form of a draconic spirit, which can manifest in physical form as a drake. As your powers grow, your drake grows as well, blossoming from a small four-legged companion to a majestic winged creature large and strong enough for you to ride. Along the way, you gain an increasing share of the awe-inspiring power of dragons.\n\nConsider the source of the draconic spirit you have bonded with. The Drakewarden Origin table offers examples.\n\nd6 | Origin\n\n1 | You studied a dragon's scale or claw, or a trinket from a dragon's hoard, creating your bond through that token's lingering draconic magic.\n\n2 | A secret order of rangers who collect and guard draconic lore taught you their ways.\n\n3 | A dragon gave you a geode or gemstone to care for. To your surprise, the drake hatched from that stone.\n\n4 | You ingested a few drops of dragon blood, forever infusing your nature magic with draconic power.\n\n5 | An ancient Draconic inscription on a standing stone empowered you when you read it aloud.\n\n6 | You had a vivid dream of a mysterious figure accompanied by seven yellow canaries, who warned you of impending doom. When you awoke, your drake was there, watching you."},
  ["creature.dralmorrer-borngray.hotdq2014"]={title="Dralmorrer Borngray",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 16 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Bullywug, Draconic, Elvish, Goblin, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nDralmorrer has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\nWar Magic\n\nWhen Dralmorrer uses his action to cast a cantrip, he can also take a bonus action to make one weapon attack.\n\nWeapon Bond\n\nProvided his longsword is on the same plane Dralmorrer can take a bonus action to teleport it to his hand.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDralmorrer attacks twice, either with his longsword or dagger.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or ranged 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.drannin-splithelm.pota2014"]={title="Drannin Splithelm",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 8 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: cold, poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAction Surge (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nDrannin takes an additional action on his turn.\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when Drannin hits with it (included in the attack).\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nDrannin has advantage on saving throws against poison.\n\nIndomitable (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nDrannin can reroll a saving throw that he fails. He must use the new roll.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nDrannin can use a bonus action to regain 16 (1d10 + 11) hit points.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nDrannin wears a control amulet for his shield guardian (see the Monster Manual) and a ring of cold resistance. He also carries a potion of frost giant strength.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDrannin makes three attacks with his greataxe.\n\nGreataxe\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["spell.drawmij-s-instant-summons.phb2014"]={title="Drawmij's Instant Summons",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\nYou touch an object weighing 10 pounds or less whose longest dimension is 6 feet or less. The spell leaves an invisible mark on its surface and invisibly inscribes the name of the item on the sapphire you use as the material component. Each time you cast this spell, you must use a different sapphire.\n\nAt any time thereafter, you can use your action to speak the item's name and crush the sapphire. The item instantly appears in your hand regardless of physical or planar distances, and the spell ends.\n\nIf another creature is holding or carrying the item, crushing the sapphire doesn't transport the item to you, but instead you learn who the creature possessing the object is and roughly where that creature is located at that moment.\n\nDispel magic or a similar effect successfully applied to the sapphire ends this spell's effect."},
  ["spell.drawmij-s-instant-summons.xphb2024"]={title="Drawmij's Instant Summons",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 266\n\nYou touch the sapphire used in the casting and an object weighing 10 pounds or less whose longest dimension is 6 feet or less. The spell leaves an XPHB mark on that object and invisibly inscribes the object's name on the sapphire. Each time you cast this spell, you must use a different sapphire.\n\nThereafter, you can take a XPHB action to speak the object's name and crush the sapphire. The object instantly appears in your hand regardless of physical or planar distances, and the spell ends.\n\nIf another creature is holding or carrying the object, crushing the sapphire doesn't transport it, but instead you learn who that creature is and where that creature is currently located."},
  ["feature.dread-allegiance.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.3"]={title="Dread Allegiance",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nChoose one of the Dead Three: Faerûnian, Faerûnian, or Faerûnian. You gain XPHB to one type of damage and the ability to cast a cantrip, as detailed in the table below; Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for this cantrip. When you finish a XPHB, you can change your choice.\n\nGod | Damage Resistance | Cantrip\n\nFaerûnian | Psychic | XPHB\n\nFaerûnian | Poison | XPHB\n\nFaerûnian | Necrotic | XPHB"},
  ["feature.dread-ambusher.xge2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Dread Ambusher",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 41\n\nAt 3rd level, you master the art of the ambush. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Wisdom modifier.\n\nAt the start of your first turn of each combat, your walking speed increases by 10 feet, which lasts until the end of that turn. If you take the Attack action on that turn, you can make one additional weapon attack as part of that action. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's damage type."},
  ["feature.dread-ambusher.xphb2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Dread Ambusher",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.dread-doppelganger.mabjov2014"]={title="Dread Doppelganger",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 22 | CON 14 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmbusher\n\nThe dread doppelganger has advantage on attack rolls against any creature it has surprised.\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe dread doppelganger can use its action to polymorph into a Small or Medium Humanoid it has seen, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the dread doppelganger surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 17 (5d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dread doppelganger makes three Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 9 to hit, range 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6).\n\nRead Thoughts\n\nThe dread doppelganger magically reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 60 feet of it. The effect can penetrate barriers, but 3 ft. of wood or dirt, 2 feet of stone, 2 inches of metal, or a thin sheet of lead blocks it. While the target is in range, the dread doppelganger can continue reading its thoughts, as long as the dread doppelganger's Concentration isn't broken (as if concentration on a spell). While reading the target's mind, the doppelganger has advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion) checks against the target."},
  ["item.dread-helm.wtthc2014"]={title="Dread Helm",subtitle="Item - WttHC - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.dread-helm.xdmg2024"]={title="Dread Helm",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhile you're wearing this fearsome steel helm, your eyes glow red and the rest of your face is hidden in shadow."},
  ["magicitem.dread-helm.xge2024"]={title="Dread Helm",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis fearsome steel helm makes your eyes glow red while you wear it."},
  ["feature.dread-incarnate.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.17"]={title="Dread Incarnate",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCutthroat\n\nYou regain one expended use of Rogue when you finish a XPHB.\n\nMurderous Intent\n\nWhen you roll for your Rogue damage, you can treat a roll of a 1 or 2 on the die as a 3."},
  ["feature.dread-lord.dmg2014.paladin.oathbreaker.20"]={title="Dread Lord",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nAt 20th level, the paladin can, as an action, surround himself or herself with an aura of gloom that lasts for 1 minute. The aura reduces any bright light in a 30-foot radius around the paladin to dim light. Whenever an enemy that is frightened by the paladin starts its turn in the aura, it takes 4d10 psychic damage. Additionally, the paladin and creatures he or she chooses in the aura are draped in deeper shadow. Creatures that rely on sight have disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures draped in this shadow.\n\nWhile the aura lasts, the paladin can use a bonus action on his or her turn to cause the shadows in the aura to attack one creature. The paladin makes a melee spell attack against the target. If the attack hits, the target takes necrotic damage equal to 3d10 + the paladin's Charisma modifier.\n\nAfter activating the aura, the paladin can't do so again until he or she finishes a long rest."},
  ["creature.dread-warrior.tftyp2014"]={title="Dread Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the dread warrior to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5+the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the dread warrior drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dread warrior makes two melee attacks.\n\nBattleaxe\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if wielded with two hands.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.dreadful-aspect.dmg2014.paladin.oathbreaker.3"]={title="Dreadful Aspect",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.dreadful-strikes.tce2014.ranger.fey-wanderer.3"]={title="Dreadful Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 58\n\n3rd-level Fey Wanderer feature\n\nYou can augment your weapon strikes with mind-scarring magic, drawn from the gloomy hollows of the Feywild. When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d4 psychic damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn.\n\nThe extra damage increases to 1d6 when you reach 11th level in this class."},
  ["feature.dreadful-strikes.xphb2024.ranger.fey-wanderer.3"]={title="Dreadful Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.dreadful-word.phb2014"]={title="Dreadful Word",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can cast confusion once using a warlock spell slot. You can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.dreadnaught.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Dreadnaught",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYou design your armor to become a towering juggernaut in battle. It has the following features:\n\n• Force Demolisher An arcane wrecking ball or sledgehammer projects from your armor. The demolisher counts as a Simple Melee weapon with the XPHB property, and it deals 1d10 Force damage on a hit. If you hit a creature that is at least one size smaller than you with the demolisher, you can push the creature up to 10 feet straight away from yourself or pull the creature up to 10 feet toward yourself.\n\n• Giant Stature As a XPHB, you transform and enlarge your armor for 1 minute. For the duration, your reach increases by 5 feet, and if you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If there isn't enough room for you to increase your size, your size doesn't change. You can use this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["spell.dream.phb2014"]={title="Dream",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 236\n\nThis spell shapes a creature's dreams. Choose a creature known to you as the target of this spell. The target must be on the same plane of existence as you. Creatures that don't sleep, such as elves, can't be contacted by this spell. You, or a willing creature you touch, enters a trance state, acting as a messenger. While in the trance, the messenger is aware of his or her surroundings, but can't take actions or move.\n\nIf the target is asleep, the messenger appears in the target's dreams and can converse with the target as long as it remains asleep, through the duration of the spell. The messenger can also shape the environment of the dream, creating landscapes, objects, and other images. The messenger can emerge from the trance at any time, ending the effect of the spell early. The target recalls the dream perfectly upon waking. If the target is awake when you cast the spell, the messenger knows it, and can either end the trance (and the spell) or wait for the target to fall asleep, at which point the messenger appears in the target's dreams.\n\nYou can make the messenger appear monstrous and terrifying to the target. If you do, the messenger can deliver a message of no more than ten words and then the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, echoes of the phantasmal monstrosity spawn a nightmare that lasts the duration of the target's sleep and prevents the target from gaining any benefit from that rest. In addition, when the target wakes up, it takes 3d6 psychic damage.\n\nIf you have a body part, lock of hair, clipping from a nail, or similar portion of the target's body, the target makes its saving throw with disadvantage."},
  ["spell.dream.xphb2024"]={title="Dream",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 266\n\nYou target a creature you know on the same plane of existence. You or a willing creature you touch enters a trance state to act as a dream messenger. While in the trance, the messenger is XPHB and has a XPHB of 0.\n\nIf the target is asleep, the messenger appears in the target's dreams and can converse with the target as long as it remains asleep, through the spell's duration. The messenger can also shape the dream's environment, creating landscapes, objects, and other images. The messenger can emerge from the trance at any time, ending the spell. The target recalls the dream perfectly upon waking.\n\nIf the target is awake when you cast the spell, the messenger knows it and can either end the trance (and the spell) or wait for the target to sleep, at which point the messenger enters its dreams.\n\nYou can make the messenger terrifying to the target. If you do so, the messenger can deliver a message of no more than ten words, and then the target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target gains no benefit from its rest, and it takes 3d6 Psychic damage when it wakes up."},
  ["creature.dream-eater.mcv2dc2014"]={title="Dream Eater",subtitle="Criatura - MCV2DC - 2014",body="Pagina: 3\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 77 (14d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 50\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 20 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 21\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGhastly Visions\n\nEach creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of the dream eater must make a 16 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is frightened of the dream eater until the start of the creature's next turn. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the creature is immune to this dream eater's Ghastly Visions trait for the next 24 hours.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe dream eater can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe dream eater has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dream eater makes two Ensnaring Shriek attacks.\n\nEnsnaring Shriek\n\nms,rs 8 to hit, reach 15 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) psychic damage, and if the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the target must succeed on a 16 Charisma saving throw or be pulled up to 15 feet toward the dream eater.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEngulfing Nightmare\n\nThe dream eater targets one creature within 5 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be engulfed by the dream eater, as the dream eater envelops the creature in a miasma of its worst fears.\n\nWhen the dream eater engulfs a target, the dream eater enters its space, and the target immediately takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage. An engulfed target is restrained and blinded, and it takes an additional 10 (3d6) psychic damage at the start of each of the dream eater's turns. When the dream eater moves, the engulfed target moves with it.\n\nThe dream eater can have only one target engulfed at a time. An engulfed target escapes at the start of its turn by making a 16 Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the target escapes; the target is no longer engulfed, and it enters a space of its choice within 5 feet of the dream eater. A creature within 15 feet of the dream eater also can use its action to attempt to free an engulfed target. Doing so requires the creature to use its action to make a 16 Charisma (Persuasion) check to convince the engulfed target the nightmare isn't real, with the target escaping on a success. The creature making the check takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage, regardless of the check's success or failure, as its mind brushes against the nightmare."},
  ["spell.dream-of-the-blue-veil.tce2014"]={title="Dream of the Blue Veil",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 7 - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 106\n\nYou and up to eight willing creatures within range fall unconscious for the spell's duration and experience visions of another world on the Material Plane, such as Oerth, Toril, Krynn, or Eberron. If the spell reaches its full duration, the visions conclude with each of you encountering and pulling back a mysterious blue curtain. The spell then ends with you mentally and physically transported to the world that was in the visions.\n\nTo cast this spell, you must have a magic item that originated on the world you wish to reach, and you must be aware of the world's existence, even if you don't know the world's name. Your destination in the other world is a safe location within 1 mile of where the magic item was created. Alternatively, you can cast the spell if one of the affected creatures was born on the other world, which causes your destination to be a safe location within 1 mile of where that creature was born.\n\nThe spell ends early on a creature if that creature takes any damage, and the creature isn't transported. If you take any damage, the spell ends for you and all the other creatures, with none of you being transported."},
  ["magicitem.dream-weaver.au2014"]={title="Dream Weaver",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis magic tapestry can be hung on a wall or another suitable vertical surface. The tapestry magically unravels and reweaves itself to illustrate the content and emotions of your most recent dreams.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while the tapestry is hung and you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nDream Wisdom\n\nDuring a XPHB, you can spend an hour studying the tapestry. At the end of the XPHB, roll 1d20 and record the number rolled. Once before you finish a XPHB, you can replace any XPHB you make with this result. You must choose to do so before you roll the XPHB.\n\nMessage Recorder\n\nIf you are targeted by the XPHB spell, the tapestry records the appearance and name of the spell's caster in its design.\n\nMind Wall\n\nWhile you have the XPHB condition, you have XPHB on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws."},
  ["creature.dreaming-dark-infiltrator.efa2014"]={title="Dreaming Dark Infiltrator",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 59\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 17 | CON 15 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Quori; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe infiltrator makes three Mind Blade attacks.\n\nMind Blade\n\nm,r 7, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nMind Curse\n\nwis 15, one creature hit by the infiltrator's Mind Blade attack this turn. actSaveFail The target takes 14 (4d6) Psychic damage and is cursed. While cursed in this way, it has XPHB on attack rolls against the infiltrator, and the infiltrator always knows its location while it and the infiltrator are on the same plane of existence. A cursed creature repeats the save whenever it finishes a XPHB or XPHB, ending the effect on itself on a success. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.dreaming-dark-mindkiller.efa2014"]={title="Dreaming Dark Mindkiller",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 180 (24d8 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 19 | CON 16 | INT 21 | WIS 18 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Quori; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSlayer's Puppet (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mindkiller makes two Nightmare Whisper attacks.\n\nNightmare Whisper\n\nm,r 9, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. h27 (5d8 + 5) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the mindkiller's next turn. If the target is already XPHB, it instead takes an extra 10 (3d6) Psychic damage.\n\nPrimal Fear (1/Day)\n\nwis 17, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the mindkiller can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 35 (10d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the mindkiller's next turn. While XPHB in this way, the target can do only one of the following on each of its turns: move, take an action, or take a XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["item.dreamlily.erlw2014"]={title="Dreamlily",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA psychoactive liquid that smells and tastes like your favorite beverage, essence of dreamlily is a Sarlonan opiate. First imported to help manage pain during the Last War, it's now the most commonly abused substance in Sharn. Though dreamlily isn't illegal if used for medicinal purposes, it's heavily taxed, and thus most dreamlily is smuggled in and sold on the black market. Dreamlily dens can be found across the lower wards. Consuming dreamlily causes disorienting euphoria and brings about remarkable resistance to pain. A creature under the effects of dreamlily is poisoned for 1 hour. While poisoned in this way, the creature is immune to fear, and the first time it drops to 0 hit points without being killed outright, it drops to 1 hit point instead. A dose of dreamlily costs around 1 gp, or up to ten times that if purchased through legal channels. There are many varieties of the drug, however, and the duration or the price might vary accordingly."},
  ["creature.drelnza.qftis2014"]={title="Drelnza",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 187 (22d8 + 88)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Giant\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Drelnza fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nDrelnza wields QftIS.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nDrelnza can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Hypersensitivity\n\nDrelnza takes 20 radiant damage when she starts her turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, she has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDrelnza makes one Bite attack and one Heretic attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the necrotic damage taken, and Drelnza regains hit points equal to that amount. The reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0. A Humanoid slain in this way and then buried rises the following night as a vampire spawn under Drelnza's control.\n\nHeretic\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft. one target. h40 (6d10 + 7) slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or have the paralyzed condition until the start of Drelnza's next turn. Celestials have disadvantage on the saving throw.\n\nCharm\n\nDrelnza targets one Humanoid she can see within 30 feet of herself. The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or have the charmed condition. While charmed in this way, the target regards Drelnza as a trusted friend to be heeded and protected. The target isn't under Drelnza's control, but it takes her requests and actions in the most favorable way.\n\nEach time Drelnza or her allies do anything harmful to the target, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. Otherwise, the effect lasts 24 hours or until Drelnza is destroyed, is on a different plane of existence than the target, or takes a bonus action to end the effect.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMove\n\nImmediately after a creature Drelnza can see ends its turn, Drelnza moves up to her speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nParry\n\nDrelnza adds 5 to her AC against one melee attack that would hit her. To do so, she must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.dretch.mm2014"]={title="Dretch",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 57\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 60 ft. (works only with creatures that understand Abyssal)\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dretch makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (2d4) slashing damage.\n\nFetid Cloud (1/Day)\n\nA 10-foot radius of disgusting green gas extends out from the dretch. The gas spreads around corners, and its area is lightly obscured. It lasts for 1 minute or until a strong wind disperses it. Any creature that starts its turn in that area must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of its next turn. While poisoned in this way, the target can take either an action or a bonus action on its turn, not both, and can't take reactions."},
  ["creature.dretch.wtthc2014"]={title="Dretch",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.dretch.xmm2024"]={title="Dretch",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 103\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal; telepathy 60 ft. (works only with creatures that understand Abyssal)\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRend\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage.\n\nFetid Cloud (1/Day)\n\ncon 11, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the dretch. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the creature can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both, and it can't take Reactions."},
  ["creature.drevin.tftyp2014"]={title="Drevin",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.drider.mm2014"]={title="Drider",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe drider has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put the drider to sleep.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe drider can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the drider has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe drider ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drider makes three attacks, either with its longsword or its longbow. It can replace one of those attacks with a bite attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h2 (1d4) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) poison damage.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage."},
  ["creature.drider.xmm2024"]={title="Drider",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 105\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 19 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe drider can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the drider has XPHB on ability checks and attack rolls.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe drider ignores movement restrictions caused by webs, and the drider knows the location of any other creature in contact with the same web.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nMagic of the Spider Queen {@recharge 5}\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drider makes three attacks, using Foreleg or Poison Burst in any combination.\n\nForeleg\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nPoison Burst\n\nr 6, range 120 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.driftglobe.dmg2014"]={title="Driftglobe",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis small sphere of thick glass weighs 1 pound. If you are within 60 feet of it, you can speak its command word and cause it to emanate the light or daylight spell. Once used, the daylight effect can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nYou can speak another command word as an action to make the illuminated globe rise into the air and float no more than 5 feet off the ground. The globe hovers in this way until you or another creature grasps it. If you move more than 60 feet from the hovering globe, it follows you until it is within 60 feet of you. It takes the shortest route to do so. If prevented from moving, the globe sinks gently to the ground and becomes inactive, and its light winks out."},
  ["magicitem.driftglobe.xdmg2024"]={title="Driftglobe",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis small sphere of thick glass weighs 1 pound. If you are within 60 feet of it, you can command it to emanate light equivalent to that of the XPHB or XPHB spell (your choice). Once used, the Daylight effect can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nYou can issue another command as a XPHB action to make the illuminated globe rise into the air and float no more than 5 feet off the ground. The globe hovers in this way until you or another creature grasps it. If you move more than 60 feet from the hovering globe, it follows you until it is within 60 feet of you. It takes the shortest route to do so. If prevented from moving, the globe sinks gently to the ground and becomes inactive, and its light winks out."},
  ["creature.drivvin-freth.wdmm2014"]={title="Drivvin Freth",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Dwarvish, Elvish, Goblin, Undercommon"},
  ["charoption.drizzt-fan.idrotf2014"]={title="Drizzt Fan",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nI once met the famous drow ranger Drizzt Do'Urden! In fact, I have a tattered piece of his famous green cloak and would never think to part with it."},
  ["creature.droki.oota2014"]={title="Droki",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 231\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 31 (7d6 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 5 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Dwarvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nDroki wears boots of speed.\n\nInsanity\n\nDroki has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened.\n\nSneak Attack (1/Turn)\n\nDroki deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage when he hits a target with a weapon attack and has advantage on the attack roll, or when the target is within 5 feet of an ally of Droki that isn't incapacitated and Droki doesn't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe derro has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the derro has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDroki makes two attacks with his shortsword\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage. The sword is coated with serpent venom that wears off after the first hit. A target subjected to the venom must make a 11 Constitution saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nDroki adds 3 to his AC against one melee attack that would hit him. To do so, Droki must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.drow.mm2014"]={title="Drow",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 13 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe drow has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put the drow to sleep.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the drow has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 hour. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target is also unconscious while poisoned in this way. The target wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature takes an action to shake it awake."},
  ["creature.drow-acolyte.oota2014"]={title="Drow Acolyte",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.drow-arachnomancer.mpmm2014"]={title="Drow Arachnomancer",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 162 (25d8 + 50)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 17 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon, can speak with spiders\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe drow has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put the drow to sleep.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe drow can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the drow has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe drow ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drow makes three attacks, using Bite, Poisonous Touch, Web, or a combination of them. One attack can be replaced by a use of Spellcasting.\n\nBite (Spider Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 31 (7d8) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the poison damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned in this way.\n\nPoisonous Touch (Humanoid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h35 (10d6) poison damage.\n\nWeb (Spider Form Only; {@recharge 5})\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one target. hThe target is restrained by webbing. As an action, the restrained target can make a 15 Strength check, bursting the webbing on a success. The webbing can also be attacked and destroyed (AC 10; hp 5; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to bludgeoning, poison, and psychic damage).\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe drow magically transforms into a Large spider, remaining in that form for up to 1 hour, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. It can speak and cast spells while in spider form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying in Humanoid form melds into the spider form. It can't activate, use, wield, or otherwise benefit from any of its equipment. It reverts to its Humanoid form if it dies."},
  ["creature.drow-arachnomancer.mtf2014"]={title="Drow Arachnomancer",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 162 (25d8 + 50)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 17 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon, can speak with spiders\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChange Shape (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe drow can use a bonus action to magically polymorph into a giant spider, remaining in that form for up to 1 hour. It can revert to its true form as a bonus action. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. It can speak and cast spells while in giant spider form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying in humanoid form melds into the giant spider form. It can't activate, use, wield, or otherwise benefit from any of its equipment. It reverts to its humanoid form if it dies.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe drow has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put the drow to sleep.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe drow can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the drow has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe drow ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drow makes two poisonous touch attacks or two bite attacks. The first of these attacks that hits each round deals an extra 26 (4d12) poison damage to the target.\n\nPoisonous Touch (Humanoid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h28 (8d6) poison damage.\n\nBite (Giant Spider Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 26 (4d12) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the poison damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned in this way.\n\nWeb (Giant Spider Form Only Recharge 5–6)\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one target. hThe target is restrained by webbing. As an action, the restrained target can make a 15 Strength check, bursting the webbing on a success. The webbing can also be attacked and destroyed (AC 10; hp 5; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to bludgeoning, poison, and psychic damage)."},
  ["creature.drow-assassin.oota2014"]={title="Drow Assassin",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 140\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
